WEBVTT

1
00:00:02,161 --> 00:00:04,230
(tense music)

2
00:00:55,948 --> 00:00:59,151
(engine revving)

3
00:01:09,395 --> 00:01:11,464
(metal crashes)

4
00:01:21,674 --> 00:01:24,176
(indistinct chatter)

5
00:01:29,815 --> 00:01:33,218
(faint thumping)

6
00:01:37,055 --> 00:01:41,093
(man speaking indistinctly)

7
00:01:41,994 --> 00:01:43,662
(keys jingling)

8
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:48,501
(clicks)

9
00:01:57,510 --> 00:01:58,544
(man over earpiece)
He's coming down.

10
00:01:59,845 --> 00:02:01,113
(telephone ringing)

11
00:02:01,213 --> 00:02:04,049
(gate opening)

12
00:02:04,850 --> 00:02:08,220
(indistinct chatter)

13
00:02:13,959 --> 00:02:15,093
(elevator bell dings)

14
00:02:20,399 --> 00:02:23,602
Well, I wanted to reassure
you and your father,

15
00:02:23,702 --> 00:02:24,737
you're in good hands.

16
00:02:25,871 --> 00:02:27,205
Ambitious...

17
00:02:27,306 --> 00:02:29,274
- How'd it go?
- Almost done.

18
00:02:29,375 --> 00:02:31,076
(businessman
speaks indistinctly)

19
00:02:41,487 --> 00:02:42,755
All this...

20
00:02:44,390 --> 00:02:45,724
began with that.

21
00:02:46,625 --> 00:02:49,127
We're gonna take great care
of your company, sir.

22
00:02:50,896 --> 00:02:51,997
I know you will.

23
00:02:55,167 --> 00:02:58,937
(businessman
speaks indistinctly)

24
00:02:59,938 --> 00:03:01,340
(car honks)

25
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:02,975
(businessman)
All right, gentlemen.

26
00:03:03,075 --> 00:03:04,977
See you in a week
when we make it official.

27
00:03:05,077 --> 00:03:06,579
Great day.

28
00:03:07,112 --> 00:03:08,280
(car door opens)

29
00:03:11,950 --> 00:03:12,918
(car door closes)

30
00:03:14,186 --> 00:03:15,354
Congrats.

31
00:03:15,454 --> 00:03:16,522
Thank you, brother.

32
00:03:36,775 --> 00:03:38,711
Relax.

33
00:03:38,811 --> 00:03:41,246
This is what you wanted.
You should be happy.

34
00:03:41,346 --> 00:03:42,448
I am.

35
00:03:43,482 --> 00:03:44,550
Are you?

36
00:03:46,985 --> 00:03:48,487
For me, it's, uh...

37
00:03:49,722 --> 00:03:50,856
bittersweet.

38
00:03:57,195 --> 00:04:00,065
(soft music)

39
00:04:24,322 --> 00:04:25,658
- (Tibu) Thank you.
- (staff speaks Thai)

40
00:04:33,566 --> 00:04:35,000
(Tibu in English) Do what
you need to do, then come over

41
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:36,769
so we can settle
our business, yeah?

42
00:04:36,869 --> 00:04:38,103
(Cole) Sure.

43
00:04:54,219 --> 00:04:56,589
- (Cole) All good?
- Yeah, all good.

44
00:04:58,256 --> 00:05:00,493
Oh, and, boss, uh,
tomorrow night's guest list

45
00:05:00,593 --> 00:05:01,694
just came through.

46
00:05:01,794 --> 00:05:02,928
It's on your tablet.

47
00:05:03,028 --> 00:05:04,697
(Cole) Thanks. I'll take a look.

48
00:05:05,798 --> 00:05:06,865
(door opens)

49
00:05:13,539 --> 00:05:15,641
How did you become
so good at this?

50
00:05:17,142 --> 00:05:21,279
When I was a rookie,
they had me work the jail.

51
00:05:23,549 --> 00:05:26,619
Best chess players in the world
live behind bars.

52
00:05:27,553 --> 00:05:28,487
Mm.

53
00:05:30,556 --> 00:05:32,324
Do you miss
being a police officer?

54
00:05:33,058 --> 00:05:34,560
I miss the action.

55
00:05:35,961 --> 00:05:37,329
Not the politics.

56
00:05:37,429 --> 00:05:38,664
- (chess piece thuds)
- Check.

57
00:05:41,133 --> 00:05:42,568
(Tibu) You can never go back?

58
00:05:43,168 --> 00:05:44,637
(Cole) No.

59
00:05:44,737 --> 00:05:46,071
I made some mistakes.

60
00:05:47,105 --> 00:05:49,341
Pissed off the wrong people.

61
00:05:49,441 --> 00:05:50,509
(inhales sharply)

62
00:05:51,644 --> 00:05:53,145
Today, um...

63
00:05:55,147 --> 00:05:56,481
would have been
your father's birthday.

64
00:05:56,582 --> 00:05:57,850
(chuckles)

65
00:05:59,251 --> 00:06:01,053
Trying to break
my concentration.

66
00:06:01,153 --> 00:06:02,521
Whatever it takes to win.

67
00:06:03,922 --> 00:06:05,658
Well, you'll need
all the help you can get.

68
00:06:05,758 --> 00:06:07,259
(chuckles)

69
00:06:12,965 --> 00:06:14,032
You're okay?

70
00:06:17,169 --> 00:06:18,136
Yeah.

71
00:06:20,505 --> 00:06:21,540
Thanks for remembering.

72
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:24,543
Oh. I wish I could have met him.

73
00:06:24,643 --> 00:06:26,044
(Cole) Yeah, you'd have
loved him.

74
00:06:27,212 --> 00:06:28,714
He was, uh...

75
00:06:31,884 --> 00:06:33,351
I mean, he could play.

76
00:06:34,653 --> 00:06:36,021
He'd have kicked your ass
worse than I do.

77
00:06:36,121 --> 00:06:38,857
- (chuckles)
- And taken your money.

78
00:06:40,225 --> 00:06:41,627
Check.

79
00:06:41,727 --> 00:06:43,028
(exhales)

80
00:06:46,064 --> 00:06:48,967
If you were me,
what would you do?

81
00:06:50,335 --> 00:06:51,837
I'd probably surrender.

82
00:06:53,371 --> 00:06:54,439
Ahh.

83
00:06:54,539 --> 00:06:56,842
(Tibu laughing)

84
00:06:57,876 --> 00:07:00,112
- But you don't have to.
- Ah.

85
00:07:00,212 --> 00:07:01,379
No, you've won.

86
00:07:01,479 --> 00:07:03,048
(both chuckle)

87
00:07:07,753 --> 00:07:09,655
(gulps, inhales)

88
00:07:09,755 --> 00:07:10,756
(smacks lips)

89
00:07:21,566 --> 00:07:22,601
(chuckles softly)

90
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:29,341
(sighs)

91
00:07:31,677 --> 00:07:33,946
(clears throat)

92
00:07:39,017 --> 00:07:40,452
Happy birthday, Dad.

93
00:07:47,092 --> 00:07:49,227
(birds chirping)

94
00:08:03,441 --> 00:08:04,877
(staff speaks Thai)

95
00:08:04,977 --> 00:08:05,978
(Kameron in English) The dinner
precedes cake cutting.

96
00:08:06,078 --> 00:08:07,012
Ready for your big night?

97
00:08:07,112 --> 00:08:08,446
My father's gonna make a speech.

98
00:08:08,546 --> 00:08:10,048
- You know how much I hate this.
- (both chuckle)

99
00:08:12,651 --> 00:08:13,852
(engine starts)

100
00:08:13,952 --> 00:08:15,120
(speaks Thai)

101
00:08:22,394 --> 00:08:24,697
(in English) Yeah. Yeah, yeah.
Yes, well, it was like, um,

102
00:08:24,797 --> 00:08:26,631
what is-- what is this language
you've been learning?

103
00:08:26,732 --> 00:08:28,366
I don't-- I don't recognize it.

104
00:08:28,466 --> 00:08:29,935
Are you sure
you've been learning?

105
00:08:30,969 --> 00:08:32,771
(muffled laughter)

106
00:08:33,605 --> 00:08:35,473
(speaking Thai)

107
00:08:35,573 --> 00:08:38,076
(all exclaim)

108
00:08:39,945 --> 00:08:41,914
(speaking Thai indistinctly)

109
00:08:44,149 --> 00:08:46,685
(chattering, laughing)

110
00:08:55,027 --> 00:08:56,862
(tapping glass)

111
00:08:58,030 --> 00:08:59,564
(in English) I have.
I have, yeah. I went last year.

112
00:08:59,664 --> 00:09:00,665
(Tibu clears throat)

113
00:09:00,766 --> 00:09:02,701
(breathes deeply)

114
00:09:02,801 --> 00:09:05,704
You spend your life
chasing success,

115
00:09:05,804 --> 00:09:08,741
only to one day realize
that all that matters

116
00:09:08,841 --> 00:09:10,843
is how you achieved it.

117
00:09:10,943 --> 00:09:12,344
What you've left behind.

118
00:09:13,712 --> 00:09:16,414
- Ours is a very dirty business.
- Who's that?

119
00:09:16,514 --> 00:09:19,752
(Tibu) But our company's
"ethics over profits" spirit...

120
00:09:19,852 --> 00:09:22,587
(Taran) Jaran Daniles.
Trans-Pacific Exports.

121
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:26,524
Cleanest record on the high seas
over the past 40 years,

122
00:09:26,624 --> 00:09:29,795
and that... is what
I am most proud of.

123
00:09:29,895 --> 00:09:32,130
- (guest 1) Yes.
- (guests clapping)

124
00:09:32,230 --> 00:09:33,565
(guest 2) Bravo.

125
00:09:36,902 --> 00:09:38,536
(Tibu) I'd like to thank you
for joining me...

126
00:09:38,636 --> 00:09:39,972
- (man) Yes. Good to meet you.
- ...and my son Kameron

127
00:09:40,072 --> 00:09:41,807
on this special occasion.

128
00:09:41,907 --> 00:09:43,408
(man) El Salvador.

129
00:09:43,508 --> 00:09:45,277
(Tibu) Tonight, we celebrate
a new chapter

130
00:09:45,377 --> 00:09:47,112
for the Campallo family.

131
00:09:47,212 --> 00:09:48,546
A new beginning.

132
00:09:49,514 --> 00:09:51,316
I'm so proud
of the work Kameron did

133
00:09:51,416 --> 00:09:52,717
to grow the business,

134
00:09:52,818 --> 00:09:55,553
to help make this sale
a reality.

135
00:09:55,653 --> 00:09:56,621
Without his efforts,
none of this

136
00:09:56,721 --> 00:09:58,423
would have been possible.

137
00:09:58,523 --> 00:10:00,558
And we did it the right way.

138
00:10:02,094 --> 00:10:03,061
Together.

139
00:10:04,529 --> 00:10:05,931
Come.

140
00:10:06,031 --> 00:10:08,066
(guests clapping and cheering)

141
00:10:13,171 --> 00:10:15,373
(guests cheering loudly)

142
00:10:23,548 --> 00:10:25,350
Now, we toast and drink.

143
00:10:25,784 --> 00:10:28,286
(cheering continues)

144
00:10:30,555 --> 00:10:32,057
(Tibu) To celebrate this day.

145
00:10:36,795 --> 00:10:38,296
The one you wanted.

146
00:10:39,531 --> 00:10:40,966
Thank you.

147
00:10:41,066 --> 00:10:42,300
- Thank you.
- (guests clapping)

148
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:44,036
Cole, where are you?

149
00:10:45,904 --> 00:10:47,873
Come. Join the family.

150
00:10:56,281 --> 00:10:57,415
Open it.

151
00:11:01,119 --> 00:11:02,487
Kameron likes the flash,

152
00:11:02,587 --> 00:11:03,989
but, uh, we prefer this, right?

153
00:11:04,089 --> 00:11:06,959
This is a watch
for a man of action. (chuckles)

154
00:11:07,993 --> 00:11:09,561
- Uh, read the back.
- (box thuds)

155
00:11:12,630 --> 00:11:14,099
What does the inscription say?

156
00:11:14,933 --> 00:11:16,068
It's a date.

157
00:11:17,102 --> 00:11:19,137
It's the day he saved my life.

158
00:11:19,237 --> 00:11:23,175
Five years ago,
he risked his life to save mine.

159
00:11:23,275 --> 00:11:24,809
I offered him a job,

160
00:11:25,610 --> 00:11:27,545
and he has since become family.

161
00:11:27,645 --> 00:11:29,781
(guests clapping)

162
00:11:32,150 --> 00:11:33,218
Thanks, Tibu.

163
00:11:33,318 --> 00:11:35,420
(Tibu) Thank you. Thank you.

164
00:11:38,023 --> 00:11:40,525
- To family.
- (guests) To family!

165
00:11:40,625 --> 00:11:43,028
(cheering)

166
00:11:44,096 --> 00:11:45,397
They're celebrating.

167
00:11:45,497 --> 00:11:46,598
But don't worry.

168
00:11:47,799 --> 00:11:49,534
The sale will be dead tonight.

169
00:11:56,474 --> 00:11:58,176
Wasn't so bad, now, was it?

170
00:11:58,276 --> 00:11:59,844
(chuckles)

171
00:11:59,945 --> 00:12:01,279
It was a wonderful night.

172
00:12:04,182 --> 00:12:05,483
Everything okay?

173
00:12:06,351 --> 00:12:07,452
Yeah.

174
00:12:08,887 --> 00:12:12,524
I just, uh, never imagined
I would ever sell the company.

175
00:12:13,525 --> 00:12:14,692
Never wanted to.

176
00:12:17,495 --> 00:12:18,730
Then why'd you do it?

177
00:12:25,837 --> 00:12:27,205
I did it for Kameron.

178
00:12:28,140 --> 00:12:29,807
KMG was, uh...

179
00:12:31,076 --> 00:12:32,610
my dream, not his.

180
00:12:33,311 --> 00:12:36,481
The shipping business
is, uh, not for him.

181
00:12:39,251 --> 00:12:42,020
I wanted to give him the chance
to chase his own dreams.

182
00:12:44,889 --> 00:12:46,591
He'll never forget it, Tibu.

183
00:12:49,894 --> 00:12:50,996
Thank you.

184
00:12:54,066 --> 00:12:55,500
Why are we going this way?

185
00:12:58,503 --> 00:13:00,672
Looks like a road closure.

186
00:13:17,122 --> 00:13:18,323
(policeman 1 speaks Thai)

187
00:13:18,423 --> 00:13:20,358
(policeman 2 speaking Thai)

188
00:13:25,030 --> 00:13:26,664
(in English) I'll back us
out of here.

189
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:30,202
(policeman 1 speaking Thai)

190
00:13:32,704 --> 00:13:34,206
- (brake squeals)
- (policeman 2 speaking Thai)

191
00:13:36,574 --> 00:13:37,642
(exclaims in Thai)

192
00:13:37,742 --> 00:13:38,710
(in English) What is this?

193
00:13:38,810 --> 00:13:39,911
(policeman 1 speaks Thai)

194
00:13:41,579 --> 00:13:43,181
(policeman 2 speaking Thai)

195
00:13:43,281 --> 00:13:44,316
(exclaims in Thai)

196
00:13:53,725 --> 00:13:54,792
- (in English) Get down!
- (gunshots)

197
00:13:54,892 --> 00:13:56,461
(yelps)

198
00:13:56,561 --> 00:13:57,929
(hitman) Take 'em down!

199
00:14:00,965 --> 00:14:02,167
(engine revving)

200
00:14:05,403 --> 00:14:06,904
- (gunshots)
- (tires screech)

201
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:10,975
- (grunts)
- (car alarm wailing)

202
00:14:11,676 --> 00:14:12,677
Ahh!

203
00:14:14,312 --> 00:14:16,014
- (gunshots)
- (hitman) Shoot the tires!

204
00:14:18,350 --> 00:14:19,984
- (car engine whirring)
- You okay?

205
00:14:20,085 --> 00:14:21,453
I'm okay.

206
00:14:27,292 --> 00:14:31,063
- (engine revving)
- (tires screeching)

207
00:14:31,163 --> 00:14:34,199
- (gunman yelling in pain)
- Ah!

208
00:14:36,101 --> 00:14:39,137
(Tibu breathing shakily)

209
00:14:42,006 --> 00:14:44,142
- (Cole) Ah, shit.
- (distant police siren wailing)

210
00:14:45,043 --> 00:14:47,179
(Tibu) What just happened?

211
00:14:47,279 --> 00:14:48,713
(shakily) Those were police.

212
00:14:51,783 --> 00:14:54,252
(shallow breathing)

213
00:14:54,352 --> 00:14:56,088
- Please...
- (Cole sighs)

214
00:14:56,188 --> 00:14:58,090
Please look after Kameron.

215
00:14:58,623 --> 00:15:01,759
(labored breathing) Look at me.

216
00:15:01,859 --> 00:15:04,129
If-- if I don't make it,
I can't help him.

217
00:15:04,229 --> 00:15:06,398
Nothing will happen to Kameron.

218
00:15:06,998 --> 00:15:09,267
- (gasping rapidly)
- Stay with me, Tibu.

219
00:15:09,367 --> 00:15:10,535
Stay with me.

220
00:15:10,635 --> 00:15:12,937
(continues gasping rapidly)

221
00:15:13,037 --> 00:15:14,005
(gasping stops)

222
00:15:18,076 --> 00:15:20,978
(emotional music)

223
00:15:35,093 --> 00:15:36,528
(cell phone rings)

224
00:15:38,062 --> 00:15:38,996
Yeah?

225
00:15:39,097 --> 00:15:40,265
(Cole over phone) Taran,

226
00:15:40,365 --> 00:15:41,799
is Kameron with you?

227
00:15:42,267 --> 00:15:44,769
(Taran) Yeah. I've got eyes
on him. He's just got back.

228
00:15:44,869 --> 00:15:47,639
Listen, we were ambushed.

229
00:15:47,739 --> 00:15:49,040
Tibu's dead.

230
00:15:50,542 --> 00:15:51,609
The fuck?

231
00:15:53,745 --> 00:15:55,012
Did you call the police?

232
00:15:55,113 --> 00:15:56,781
The police are involved.

233
00:15:56,881 --> 00:15:58,550
We can't trust anybody.

234
00:16:01,453 --> 00:16:02,954
(zipper unzips)

235
00:16:05,357 --> 00:16:07,125
One of these guys was American.

236
00:16:07,225 --> 00:16:08,693
US passport.

237
00:16:08,793 --> 00:16:11,296
- 6573247. Run it.
- (cell phone thuds)

238
00:16:12,464 --> 00:16:14,366
3247.

239
00:16:14,466 --> 00:16:15,767
Checking. Stand by.

240
00:16:16,868 --> 00:16:19,137
I've got him. Jonathan Rogers.

241
00:16:19,237 --> 00:16:21,072
Former marine. MARSOC.

242
00:16:22,407 --> 00:16:24,376
Rogers is a crewman for the KMG.

243
00:16:25,042 --> 00:16:26,678
He works for us.

244
00:16:26,778 --> 00:16:28,946
He's departing
on the Artemis tonight.

245
00:16:29,046 --> 00:16:30,715
It's gonna leave port
in two hours.

246
00:16:31,749 --> 00:16:32,884
What's your plan?

247
00:16:33,818 --> 00:16:35,220
(Cole) I'm headed to the port.

248
00:16:36,488 --> 00:16:37,955
I'll find out who did this.

249
00:16:41,493 --> 00:16:43,661
(indistinct chattering
on tablet)

250
00:16:44,962 --> 00:16:46,564
Campallo is dead, sir.

251
00:16:47,765 --> 00:16:48,800
Good.

252
00:16:50,902 --> 00:16:53,471
So, what do you want?

253
00:16:53,571 --> 00:16:54,939
We have a problem, sir.

254
00:16:56,241 --> 00:16:57,609
His bodyguard got away.

255
00:17:04,916 --> 00:17:06,818
Tell the police
to put out an APB.

256
00:17:08,286 --> 00:17:10,322
But... one more thing.

257
00:17:12,257 --> 00:17:13,958
Don't bring him in alive.

258
00:17:19,831 --> 00:17:21,766
(reporter on TV) Two police
officers were murdered tonight

259
00:17:21,866 --> 00:17:24,402
while performing
a routine traffic stop.

260
00:17:24,502 --> 00:17:27,905
Billionaire shipping tycoon
Manuel Tibu Campallo

261
00:17:28,005 --> 00:17:29,941
- was also killed.
- (gift wrapper rustles)

262
00:17:30,041 --> 00:17:32,244
The suspect
is a British citizen

263
00:17:32,344 --> 00:17:33,745
named Cole Reed.

264
00:17:33,845 --> 00:17:37,014
Reed worked as
Campallo's personal bodyguard.

265
00:17:37,982 --> 00:17:41,753
The suspect is very dangerous
and still on the loose.

266
00:17:41,853 --> 00:17:44,756
A citywide order to shelter
is in place until--

267
00:17:44,856 --> 00:17:46,558
(buzzing)

268
00:17:46,658 --> 00:17:50,962
(continues buzzing)

269
00:17:51,062 --> 00:17:52,597
- This is Ellis.
- (man over phone) Miss Ellis,

270
00:17:52,697 --> 00:17:54,232
we need you
to report immediately.

271
00:17:54,866 --> 00:17:57,369
- Well, I, um--
- The Artemis is short crew.

272
00:17:57,469 --> 00:17:58,870
Departs at midnight.

273
00:17:58,970 --> 00:18:00,104
We need you there now.

274
00:18:01,005 --> 00:18:03,575
Sir, I just got in
from the Venus San Diego haul,

275
00:18:03,675 --> 00:18:06,944
24 days across, and my flight,
well, it's in, uh,

276
00:18:07,044 --> 00:18:08,145
my flight home's in three hours.

277
00:18:08,246 --> 00:18:09,247
Miss Ellis, you're still

278
00:18:09,347 --> 00:18:11,148
a probationary employee.

279
00:18:11,249 --> 00:18:14,352
Sir, I-I have my daughter
this weekend in LA.

280
00:18:14,452 --> 00:18:16,588
Listen, if you're not
at your post

281
00:18:16,688 --> 00:18:18,390
on the Artemis in an hour,

282
00:18:18,490 --> 00:18:20,258
KMG's gonna have to let you go.

283
00:18:20,358 --> 00:18:21,526
(scoffs)

284
00:18:22,159 --> 00:18:24,262
Okay. Roger that.

285
00:18:25,897 --> 00:18:26,931
Fuck.

286
00:18:27,532 --> 00:18:28,566
Fuck.

287
00:18:29,734 --> 00:18:31,102
(exhales) Oh, fuck.

288
00:18:41,045 --> 00:18:42,614
(Cole exhales sharply)

289
00:18:59,230 --> 00:19:01,799
(keypad beeping)

290
00:19:01,899 --> 00:19:04,936
(beeping continues)

291
00:19:06,571 --> 00:19:09,607
(door opens, closes)

292
00:19:11,876 --> 00:19:14,211
Kameron,
Detective Jamai is here.

293
00:19:15,913 --> 00:19:17,382
- (Kameron) Evening, Detective.
- Good evening.

294
00:19:17,482 --> 00:19:18,816
(Kameron) Evening, Officer.

295
00:19:18,916 --> 00:19:19,884
My condolences.

296
00:19:19,984 --> 00:19:20,985
Thank you.

297
00:19:21,085 --> 00:19:22,854
I am sorry, but we are going

298
00:19:22,954 --> 00:19:24,556
to have to ask you
a few questions.

299
00:19:24,656 --> 00:19:26,724
- (sniffles) Of course. Ah...
- (phone buzzes)

300
00:19:26,824 --> 00:19:28,225
(continues buzzing)

301
00:19:28,326 --> 00:19:29,694
Uh, Taran, could you pour
these gentlemen

302
00:19:29,794 --> 00:19:31,228
- a drink, please?
- Of course.

303
00:19:31,329 --> 00:19:33,365
Hello? Who is this?

304
00:19:33,465 --> 00:19:34,932
(over phone) Kameron, it's Cole.

305
00:19:36,734 --> 00:19:37,669
Listen.

306
00:19:39,571 --> 00:19:40,838
Your father, uh...

307
00:19:43,741 --> 00:19:44,676
(inhales)

308
00:19:46,143 --> 00:19:47,345
I'm so sorry.

309
00:19:48,279 --> 00:19:49,614
(sighs) I tried.

310
00:19:51,148 --> 00:19:53,418
The police are here
asking questions.

311
00:19:53,518 --> 00:19:55,252
On the news,
they're saying you killed him.

312
00:19:55,353 --> 00:19:56,821
That's not what happened.

313
00:19:58,356 --> 00:19:59,491
We were ambushed.

314
00:20:00,525 --> 00:20:01,926
You need to stay locked down.

315
00:20:02,794 --> 00:20:05,763
Whoever killed Tibu
will be coming for you next.

316
00:20:11,302 --> 00:20:12,504
(exhales, sniffles)

317
00:20:12,604 --> 00:20:14,806
(police siren wails in distance)

318
00:20:22,179 --> 00:20:23,280
(phone thuds)

319
00:20:31,155 --> 00:20:32,557
(port guard 1 speaking Thai)

320
00:20:32,657 --> 00:20:35,126
(indistinct announcement
over PA)

321
00:20:42,366 --> 00:20:43,635
(siren wails)

322
00:20:45,970 --> 00:20:48,840
(speaking Thai over radio)

323
00:20:52,376 --> 00:20:56,213
(port security speaking in Thai)

324
00:20:57,314 --> 00:20:59,851
(tense music)

325
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:05,657
(port guard 2 speaking Thai)

326
00:21:10,995 --> 00:21:12,396
(keyboard clacks)

327
00:21:13,531 --> 00:21:15,066
(port guard 1 in English)
Make your way through security

328
00:21:15,166 --> 00:21:16,267
on your right.

329
00:21:18,603 --> 00:21:21,773
(port worker 1 speaks Thai)

330
00:21:30,582 --> 00:21:34,652
(indistinct chatter)

331
00:21:35,252 --> 00:21:36,788
(port worker 2 speaks Thai)

332
00:21:59,944 --> 00:22:00,978
(device beeps)

333
00:22:01,779 --> 00:22:02,747
(port worker 3 speaks Thai)

334
00:22:07,151 --> 00:22:08,686
(port worker 2 speaks Thai)

335
00:22:09,286 --> 00:22:12,323
(port worker talks indistinctly)

336
00:22:17,562 --> 00:22:18,830
(crewman in English)
Hey, Jonathan!

337
00:22:24,068 --> 00:22:26,504
(tense music continues)

338
00:22:29,907 --> 00:22:31,843
(keypad beeping)

339
00:22:31,943 --> 00:22:33,945
(news alert tune plays)

340
00:22:34,045 --> 00:22:35,713
(reporter on TV) For more
on this developing story,

341
00:22:35,813 --> 00:22:38,215
we go live to Stan Beckwith
on the scene.

342
00:22:38,315 --> 00:22:40,151
(Stan) New details
are emerging tonight

343
00:22:40,251 --> 00:22:42,554
following a shooting
in downtown Bangkok.

344
00:22:42,654 --> 00:22:44,088
Sources say
the incident may have been

345
00:22:44,188 --> 00:22:45,356
an attempted kidnapping

346
00:22:45,456 --> 00:22:47,091
targeting KMG CEO

347
00:22:47,191 --> 00:22:49,093
Manuel Tibu Campallo,

348
00:22:49,193 --> 00:22:51,428
allegedly carried out
by his longtime bodyguard,

349
00:22:51,529 --> 00:22:52,730
Cole Reed.

350
00:22:52,830 --> 00:22:54,198
Campallo was pronounced dead

351
00:22:54,298 --> 00:22:55,366
at the scene.

352
00:22:55,466 --> 00:22:56,433
Captain. (knocks)

353
00:22:58,002 --> 00:22:59,103
You may enter.

354
00:23:00,171 --> 00:23:03,575
- Is everybody on board?
- Yes, sir. We're good.

355
00:23:04,275 --> 00:23:06,110
Who are you, and what are you
doing on my bridge?

356
00:23:06,210 --> 00:23:07,945
(Mateo) New third mate, Captain.

357
00:23:08,045 --> 00:23:09,046
I don't need a third mate.

358
00:23:09,146 --> 00:23:11,015
I have 20 good men on board.

359
00:23:11,115 --> 00:23:12,617
Well, Captain,
I didn't wanna be here either,

360
00:23:12,717 --> 00:23:14,919
but, uh, company asked me
to report.

361
00:23:15,019 --> 00:23:16,087
Rama called in sick, sir.

362
00:23:16,187 --> 00:23:17,488
KMG sent her.

363
00:23:19,891 --> 00:23:21,158
(exhales sharply)

364
00:23:23,795 --> 00:23:26,898
(smacks lips)
Would you like me to twirl, sir?

365
00:23:29,567 --> 00:23:31,068
I'm not a fan of attitude.

366
00:23:31,168 --> 00:23:33,404
Oh, no, neither am I. At all.

367
00:23:36,040 --> 00:23:38,576
(paper rustles softly)

368
00:23:41,045 --> 00:23:44,148
Well, if the company,
in all its genius,

369
00:23:44,248 --> 00:23:46,651
wants you here,
then welcome on board.

370
00:23:47,551 --> 00:23:48,986
(Angie) I like
your necklace, sir.

371
00:23:52,023 --> 00:23:53,625
- You know what it is?
- I do.

372
00:23:53,725 --> 00:23:56,560
That is a Viking symbol
of guidance and protection.

373
00:24:00,064 --> 00:24:01,899
Impressive. Theo.

374
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:04,335
Can you take the young lady
to her cabin?

375
00:24:04,435 --> 00:24:05,502
(Theo) Sir.

376
00:24:06,370 --> 00:24:07,404
(Angie) Thank you.

377
00:24:09,240 --> 00:24:10,274
You're welcome.

378
00:24:16,080 --> 00:24:17,314
Anything else, sir?

379
00:24:17,849 --> 00:24:20,517
(Marko sighs) The two of you
are on the night shift.

380
00:24:20,618 --> 00:24:21,853
Keep an eye on her.

381
00:24:29,126 --> 00:24:31,796
(tense music)

382
00:25:08,432 --> 00:25:10,768
(horn blaring)

383
00:25:14,505 --> 00:25:16,908
- Hard to starboard!
- (Theo) Hard to starboard.

384
00:25:18,743 --> 00:25:20,577
Hard to starboard now.

385
00:25:29,821 --> 00:25:32,690
(dramatic music)

386
00:25:42,166 --> 00:25:43,267
(exhales)

387
00:26:24,842 --> 00:26:26,410
- (knock on door)
- Yeah?

388
00:26:26,510 --> 00:26:28,679
(Mateo) Captain has us
on night shift.

389
00:26:28,780 --> 00:26:30,481
All right, I'll be there
in a sec.

390
00:26:35,086 --> 00:26:37,354
(dramatic music continues)

391
00:27:13,524 --> 00:27:15,426
(radio feedback squeals,
static crackles)

392
00:27:24,936 --> 00:27:27,271
(muffled sobbing)

393
00:27:27,371 --> 00:27:30,141
(muffled thudding)

394
00:27:30,241 --> 00:27:32,076
(woman speaks indistinctly)

395
00:27:37,081 --> 00:27:39,450
(lever handle creaking, thuds)

396
00:27:40,918 --> 00:27:43,454
(metal groaning)

397
00:27:49,226 --> 00:27:52,663
(faint thumping)

398
00:27:57,234 --> 00:28:00,171
(thumping continues)

399
00:28:04,175 --> 00:28:08,079
(metal groaning)

400
00:28:18,990 --> 00:28:20,824
(woman speaks indistinctly)

401
00:28:27,031 --> 00:28:29,934
(muffled thudding)

402
00:28:30,034 --> 00:28:31,435
(woman speaks indistinctly)

403
00:28:31,535 --> 00:28:33,437
(muffled thudding)

404
00:28:39,443 --> 00:28:42,346
(metal groaning)

405
00:28:44,515 --> 00:28:47,551
(suspenseful music)

406
00:28:53,790 --> 00:28:57,661
(muffled sobbing)

407
00:29:02,466 --> 00:29:03,667
(woman speaks indistinctly)

408
00:29:07,171 --> 00:29:08,872
(muffled cry)

409
00:29:08,973 --> 00:29:10,007
(flashlight clicks)

410
00:29:11,742 --> 00:29:13,510
(Cole exhales sharply)

411
00:29:15,412 --> 00:29:16,380
(flashlight clicks)

412
00:29:18,382 --> 00:29:20,784
(clattering)

413
00:29:20,884 --> 00:29:22,086
(clunks)

414
00:29:29,994 --> 00:29:31,762
(clunks)

415
00:29:34,731 --> 00:29:36,700
- (thud)
- (door squeaks)

416
00:29:39,503 --> 00:29:42,406
(all gasp, whimper)

417
00:29:51,282 --> 00:29:53,484
- (woman mumbles)
- (Cole) It's okay.

418
00:29:53,584 --> 00:29:55,886
It's okay. I'm here to help.

419
00:29:57,721 --> 00:29:59,023
How did you get here?

420
00:29:59,123 --> 00:30:00,857
Does anyone speak English?

421
00:30:00,958 --> 00:30:03,094
Doctor. Doctor.

422
00:30:03,194 --> 00:30:04,461
Doctor.

423
00:30:07,064 --> 00:30:08,599
You speak English?

424
00:30:08,699 --> 00:30:10,667
(man coughs)

425
00:30:10,767 --> 00:30:12,403
How long have you been in here?

426
00:30:13,104 --> 00:30:14,138
Bangkok.

427
00:30:14,238 --> 00:30:15,472
They say they let us out

428
00:30:15,572 --> 00:30:17,274
as soon as leave port,

429
00:30:17,374 --> 00:30:19,510
but they leave us in dark.

430
00:30:19,610 --> 00:30:21,845
- Hot, dark.
- (Cole) Wait, wait.

431
00:30:21,945 --> 00:30:23,880
Please. Sit down.

432
00:30:24,815 --> 00:30:26,183
We need to be quiet.

433
00:30:26,283 --> 00:30:29,720
(speaks Thai)

434
00:30:29,820 --> 00:30:31,455
(Cole in English)
I'm gonna help you.

435
00:30:31,922 --> 00:30:33,257
I'm gonna bring you water...

436
00:30:34,225 --> 00:30:35,626
and food.

437
00:30:35,726 --> 00:30:37,561
Some medical supplies.

438
00:30:37,661 --> 00:30:38,662
(Seng breathes shakily)

439
00:30:38,762 --> 00:30:42,033
(translating in Thai)

440
00:30:42,133 --> 00:30:43,400
(Angie in English) Hello?

441
00:30:45,836 --> 00:30:47,404
(Cole whispering)
You need to trust me.

442
00:30:47,504 --> 00:30:50,674
I'm coming back. For everybody.

443
00:30:50,774 --> 00:30:51,808
Okay?

444
00:30:53,610 --> 00:30:55,079
(lever handle thuds)

445
00:30:55,179 --> 00:30:56,180
(Angie) Hello?

446
00:30:56,280 --> 00:30:59,483
(metal groaning)

447
00:31:07,091 --> 00:31:08,525
Hello?

448
00:31:09,960 --> 00:31:11,428
Is anybody down here?

449
00:31:29,680 --> 00:31:32,083
- (thud)
- (door squeaking)

450
00:31:32,183 --> 00:31:34,351
- (Angie) Oh, my God.
- (all gasp)

451
00:31:34,451 --> 00:31:36,387
Oh, my God. (sniffles)

452
00:31:36,487 --> 00:31:39,390
Okay. It's-it's-- it's okay.
C-come.

453
00:31:39,490 --> 00:31:40,791
Come. One by one.

454
00:31:42,293 --> 00:31:45,196
All right, just-just--
just stay in this area, okay?

455
00:31:45,296 --> 00:31:46,397
We'll help you.

456
00:31:47,198 --> 00:31:48,899
Okay. (breathes sharply)

457
00:31:48,999 --> 00:31:51,202
- Mateo?
- (radio static crackles)

458
00:31:52,002 --> 00:31:53,070
Fuck.

459
00:31:54,071 --> 00:31:56,773
Oh, God.
Your daughter's injured.

460
00:31:56,873 --> 00:31:58,742
Okay, is-is--
is anybody else injured?

461
00:31:59,776 --> 00:32:02,146
(Seng speaks Thai)

462
00:32:02,246 --> 00:32:03,580
(woman coughs)

463
00:32:03,680 --> 00:32:04,981
(in English)
Uh, you with the man?

464
00:32:05,082 --> 00:32:07,918
Uh, he get us food and water

465
00:32:08,018 --> 00:32:09,420
a-and medicine for my daughter.

466
00:32:09,520 --> 00:32:12,389
(Angie) What? W-what man? No.

467
00:32:12,489 --> 00:32:15,492
Look, just... stay calm.
We're gonna help you, all right?

468
00:32:15,592 --> 00:32:17,861
We're gonna get you food and
water. Just-- just stay calm.

469
00:32:18,695 --> 00:32:20,331
Josef!

470
00:32:20,431 --> 00:32:21,832
What's happening?

471
00:32:21,932 --> 00:32:23,467
These people need water
and a medic, all right?

472
00:32:23,567 --> 00:32:24,968
I'm gonna wake the captain.
Go help them.

473
00:32:25,702 --> 00:32:28,305
- Come on, go!
- Yes, I'll-- I'll handle it.

474
00:32:28,405 --> 00:32:31,342
(men whispering)

475
00:32:34,578 --> 00:32:36,713
(knocking on door)

476
00:32:37,848 --> 00:32:39,350
- (water splashes)
- (razor clangs)

477
00:32:39,450 --> 00:32:42,519
(Angie continues knocking)
Captain. Captain!

478
00:32:42,619 --> 00:32:44,155
- (water splashes)
- (razor clangs)

479
00:32:44,255 --> 00:32:45,622
(Angie knocks) Captain?

480
00:32:45,722 --> 00:32:46,790
Hold on.

481
00:32:50,026 --> 00:32:51,094
(towel thumps)

482
00:32:51,562 --> 00:32:52,796
- What is it?
- Captain,

483
00:32:52,896 --> 00:32:54,165
we found
a few dozen people locked

484
00:32:54,265 --> 00:32:55,299
in a container
in the lower hold.

485
00:32:55,399 --> 00:32:57,668
What? Come on in. Come on in.

486
00:32:57,768 --> 00:32:59,836
- They're not in good shape.
- What?

487
00:32:59,936 --> 00:33:02,339
- What-- what's going on?
- They're dehydrated. They're--

488
00:33:02,439 --> 00:33:04,275
(sighs)
Fuck, there's a little girl.

489
00:33:04,375 --> 00:33:05,809
Jesus Christ.

490
00:33:05,909 --> 00:33:07,211
Simon and Josef,
they're down there with them.

491
00:33:07,311 --> 00:33:08,645
- That's good. That's very good.
- Yeah.

492
00:33:08,745 --> 00:33:10,814
Now, calm down
and relax a little bit.

493
00:33:10,914 --> 00:33:12,283
- I'm calm.
- Have a seat.

494
00:33:15,152 --> 00:33:16,653
Captain to bridge.

495
00:33:16,753 --> 00:33:18,322
(Mateo over radio)
Go ahead, sir.

496
00:33:18,422 --> 00:33:19,790
Ellis found some people locked

497
00:33:19,890 --> 00:33:22,193
in one of the lower
container holds.

498
00:33:22,293 --> 00:33:23,627
She's here with me now.

499
00:33:24,060 --> 00:33:25,862
Let's follow protocol.

500
00:33:25,962 --> 00:33:27,097
Yes, sir.

501
00:33:28,965 --> 00:33:29,933
(radio thuds)

502
00:33:30,667 --> 00:33:32,836
- We should call the navy, sir.
- Yes, I will.

503
00:33:32,936 --> 00:33:35,071
But let's find out
what's going on first.

504
00:33:35,172 --> 00:33:37,073
I think it's pretty clear
what's going on, sir.

505
00:33:37,174 --> 00:33:39,176
I hear you, and we got this.

506
00:33:39,276 --> 00:33:40,577
I'm gonna get a hold
of the doctor

507
00:33:40,677 --> 00:33:42,012
and you can guide him down,
okay?

508
00:33:42,112 --> 00:33:43,247
- Jones for Captain.
- Sit down and relax.

509
00:33:43,347 --> 00:33:44,548
You did a good job.

510
00:33:44,648 --> 00:33:46,283
Very good. Please sit down.

511
00:33:47,484 --> 00:33:48,452
Sure.

512
00:33:49,520 --> 00:33:51,021
Marko. Come in.

513
00:33:51,121 --> 00:33:52,689
Do you need assistance, sir?

514
00:33:53,357 --> 00:33:55,226
No. Ellis is with me.

515
00:33:55,992 --> 00:33:58,529
And Mateo is-- is handling
protocol below.

516
00:33:59,863 --> 00:34:02,165
Maintain your position, please.
Thank you.

517
00:34:02,266 --> 00:34:03,600
Roger that, sir.

518
00:34:07,671 --> 00:34:10,274
(Josef) Everyone, get back
in the container. Let's go.

519
00:34:10,374 --> 00:34:11,542
(migrants speaking Thai)

520
00:34:11,642 --> 00:34:13,544
(Josef in English)
All of you, move.

521
00:34:13,644 --> 00:34:15,512
Get the fuck back inside.

522
00:34:15,612 --> 00:34:16,547
Now!

523
00:34:17,481 --> 00:34:19,182
(migrants yelping)

524
00:34:19,283 --> 00:34:21,418
- I said, get back in.
- (Simon) Get back!

525
00:34:21,518 --> 00:34:23,086
- (Josef) I said, get back in!
- (migrants screaming)

526
00:34:23,186 --> 00:34:25,021
Get back in the container!

527
00:34:25,722 --> 00:34:27,791
- Get back!
- (woman yelping)

528
00:34:30,060 --> 00:34:31,094
(migrants continue screaming)

529
00:34:31,194 --> 00:34:32,729
I said, get back in!

530
00:34:33,964 --> 00:34:35,299
(Seng gasps)

531
00:34:36,733 --> 00:34:39,069
(Josef grunting)

532
00:34:41,037 --> 00:34:42,906
- You!
- (speaks Thai)

533
00:34:43,006 --> 00:34:44,475
(grunting)

534
00:34:44,575 --> 00:34:47,344
Aah! (yelling in pain)

535
00:34:48,512 --> 00:34:50,881
(grunting)

536
00:34:50,981 --> 00:34:51,982
(gunshots)

537
00:34:56,520 --> 00:34:57,488
(grunts)

538
00:35:03,159 --> 00:35:04,961
(grunts, whimpers)

539
00:35:05,662 --> 00:35:06,930
(in English) Hey,
something's not right.

540
00:35:07,030 --> 00:35:08,465
We need to call the navy.

541
00:35:08,565 --> 00:35:09,833
- The captain just isn't--
- (gun cocks)

542
00:35:10,534 --> 00:35:12,002
(Mateo) We're not calling
anybody.

543
00:35:13,036 --> 00:35:14,004
(radio beeps)

544
00:35:15,071 --> 00:35:16,172
Mateo to Captain.

545
00:35:17,341 --> 00:35:18,475
Go for Captain.

546
00:35:18,575 --> 00:35:19,610
Got her on the bridge.

547
00:35:20,611 --> 00:35:21,878
I'm on my way.

548
00:35:23,414 --> 00:35:24,381
(knife rasps)

549
00:35:25,582 --> 00:35:28,685
- (yells)
- (both grunting)

550
00:35:28,785 --> 00:35:32,188
- (Josef groans in pain)
- (both grunting)

551
00:35:32,289 --> 00:35:33,590
(grunts)

552
00:35:35,592 --> 00:35:38,762
(both grunting)

553
00:35:39,296 --> 00:35:40,697
Step back.

554
00:35:40,797 --> 00:35:42,599
- Sit the fuck down.
- Okay.

555
00:35:42,699 --> 00:35:43,934
- (radio static crackles)
- (Angie grunts)

556
00:35:44,034 --> 00:35:46,437
- (gun clatters)
- (both grunting)

557
00:35:51,708 --> 00:35:55,278
(both grunting)

558
00:35:55,379 --> 00:35:57,113
(Josef straining)

559
00:35:57,213 --> 00:35:59,616
- Aah! (grunts)
- (Cole grunts)

560
00:35:59,716 --> 00:36:01,585
(screaming in pain)

561
00:36:03,720 --> 00:36:06,457
(yells, grunts in pain)

562
00:36:06,557 --> 00:36:07,791
(migrants screaming)

563
00:36:07,891 --> 00:36:09,693
(Dara speaks Thai)

564
00:36:09,793 --> 00:36:10,827
(gunshots)

565
00:36:12,996 --> 00:36:13,964
(Simon) Aah!

566
00:36:22,939 --> 00:36:24,174
(in English) We need to get you
off of this ship

567
00:36:24,274 --> 00:36:25,742
before the rest of them
get here.

568
00:36:26,309 --> 00:36:28,311
We need to go up
to the lifeboats.

569
00:36:28,412 --> 00:36:30,547
Stay close. Stay behind me.

570
00:36:30,647 --> 00:36:31,782
Let's move.

571
00:36:32,849 --> 00:36:35,452
(migrants conversing in Thai)

572
00:36:38,755 --> 00:36:40,791
(tense music)

573
00:36:41,992 --> 00:36:42,993
Fuck.

574
00:36:43,093 --> 00:36:44,094
(beeps)

575
00:36:44,194 --> 00:36:46,497
(signal beeping)

576
00:37:06,783 --> 00:37:07,784
(Angie) Aah!

577
00:37:08,985 --> 00:37:09,953
(Angie grunts)

578
00:37:10,487 --> 00:37:11,555
Come on.

579
00:37:14,958 --> 00:37:16,427
- Go fucking get her. Now.
- (crewman) Yes, sir.

580
00:37:16,527 --> 00:37:17,761
- Move!
- (Mateo groaning)

581
00:37:17,861 --> 00:37:20,296
What the fuck are you doing?
Get up!

582
00:37:20,397 --> 00:37:22,966
What the fuck's wrong
with you, huh?

583
00:37:23,066 --> 00:37:24,334
(Mateo)
It's still transmitting, sir.

584
00:37:24,435 --> 00:37:25,869
(Marko) Then cancel it,
you idiot.

585
00:37:25,969 --> 00:37:27,871
- (buttons click)
- Signal canceled, sir.

586
00:37:27,971 --> 00:37:29,205
We're okay.

587
00:37:29,305 --> 00:37:31,141
We're pretty fucking far
from okay.

588
00:37:31,241 --> 00:37:33,143
Now, get your sorry ass down
and disable the lifeboats

589
00:37:33,243 --> 00:37:34,244
so she can't get away.

590
00:37:34,344 --> 00:37:35,412
Yes, sir.

591
00:37:36,913 --> 00:37:38,081
And where the fuck is Jonathan?

592
00:37:38,181 --> 00:37:40,216
I'm on it, sir. Jorge, come in.

593
00:37:40,316 --> 00:37:42,753
(tense music continues)

594
00:37:53,897 --> 00:37:55,231
Ah! Fuck.

595
00:38:01,037 --> 00:38:02,338
Come on.

596
00:38:02,439 --> 00:38:03,540
Hey, you.

597
00:38:05,776 --> 00:38:07,243
You know how to use
one of these things?

598
00:38:07,343 --> 00:38:08,278
Yes.

599
00:38:09,279 --> 00:38:10,781
- Okay, listen.
- (Seng mumbles in Thai)

600
00:38:10,881 --> 00:38:12,516
I'm gonna look
for the woman who found you.

601
00:38:12,616 --> 00:38:14,284
I think she might be in trouble.

602
00:38:14,384 --> 00:38:16,587
- Don't wait for me.
- Okay.

603
00:38:28,732 --> 00:38:30,366
Captain on the bridge.

604
00:38:30,467 --> 00:38:31,702
(Spencer) As you were.

605
00:38:32,302 --> 00:38:34,337
- Good morning.
- Morning, sir.

606
00:38:34,437 --> 00:38:36,540
Distress call came in
from a cargo ship.

607
00:38:36,640 --> 00:38:38,475
KMG Artemis.

608
00:38:38,575 --> 00:38:40,176
Nine degrees, 49 minutes north,

609
00:38:40,276 --> 00:38:42,613
92 degrees, 56 minutes east.

610
00:38:42,713 --> 00:38:44,615
05:33 hours local time.

611
00:38:44,715 --> 00:38:47,317
That's the edge
of the Andaman Sea.

612
00:38:47,417 --> 00:38:49,620
- What was the code?
- Attack, sir.

613
00:38:50,386 --> 00:38:52,723
An attack? By who?

614
00:38:52,823 --> 00:38:54,558
Last I checked,
we were 600 miles east

615
00:38:54,658 --> 00:38:55,659
of any pirate activity.

616
00:38:55,759 --> 00:38:56,893
They canceled the call

617
00:38:56,993 --> 00:38:58,695
before we could respond.

618
00:38:58,795 --> 00:39:00,463
Must have been
some kind of mistake.

619
00:39:01,264 --> 00:39:02,966
(clicks tongue, inhales sharply)

620
00:39:03,066 --> 00:39:04,735
Let's give 'em a call back,
Yates.

621
00:39:04,835 --> 00:39:07,070
- Make sure everything's kosher.
- Yes, sir.

622
00:39:09,606 --> 00:39:11,041
Artemis, Artemis, Artemis.

623
00:39:11,141 --> 00:39:14,545
This is the USS Hazard Perry
on Channel 16.

624
00:39:14,645 --> 00:39:16,379
(over radio)
Artemis, Artemis, Artemis.

625
00:39:16,479 --> 00:39:19,750
This is the USS Hazard Perry
on Channel 16.

626
00:39:19,850 --> 00:39:21,585
- Artemis, Artemis, Artemis.
- Tsk.

627
00:39:22,318 --> 00:39:23,353
(radio beeps)

628
00:39:23,453 --> 00:39:25,321
Hazard Perry, this is Artemis.

629
00:39:26,923 --> 00:39:28,692
Good morning.
This is Captain Spencer

630
00:39:28,792 --> 00:39:31,194
of the USS Hazard Perry.
Who am I talking to?

631
00:39:31,762 --> 00:39:34,497
This is Marko Madsen,
captain of the Artemis.

632
00:39:34,598 --> 00:39:36,567
You must have gotten
our DSC call.

633
00:39:36,667 --> 00:39:37,701
(Spencer over radio)
Yeah, we sure did.

634
00:39:37,801 --> 00:39:38,935
So, what happened there?

635
00:39:39,469 --> 00:39:40,537
I'm sorry, one of my guys

636
00:39:40,637 --> 00:39:42,338
spotted light in our wake.

637
00:39:42,438 --> 00:39:43,840
He had a run-in
with some Somalis

638
00:39:43,940 --> 00:39:45,241
a few years ago.

639
00:39:45,341 --> 00:39:46,309
You know how that goes.

640
00:39:46,409 --> 00:39:47,410
Got a little trigger-happy

641
00:39:47,510 --> 00:39:49,112
with the DSC.

642
00:39:49,212 --> 00:39:50,981
But it turns out,
it was just a fishing vessel.

643
00:39:53,784 --> 00:39:55,952
You're pretty far out for
a fishing vessel, aren't you?

644
00:39:57,487 --> 00:39:59,389
Must-- must have been
a deep-sea trawler.

645
00:39:59,489 --> 00:40:00,891
Not the first one we see.

646
00:40:02,859 --> 00:40:04,728
Sorry to waste the navy's time.

647
00:40:07,731 --> 00:40:10,166
Not at all.
Glad everyone's okay.

648
00:40:12,903 --> 00:40:13,870
(radio thuds)

649
00:40:16,172 --> 00:40:18,374
(Jamai) You have no idea
where he could be?

650
00:40:18,474 --> 00:40:19,610
No clue, I'm afraid.

651
00:40:19,710 --> 00:40:20,777
We have a call to you

652
00:40:20,877 --> 00:40:22,145
from a burner phone,

653
00:40:22,245 --> 00:40:24,114
shortly after the accident,

654
00:40:24,214 --> 00:40:25,315
near the port.

655
00:40:27,083 --> 00:40:28,151
Who called you?

656
00:40:29,552 --> 00:40:31,454
I... don't recall.

657
00:40:32,255 --> 00:40:33,990
To be honest, I--
I don't even remember

658
00:40:34,090 --> 00:40:35,225
receiving the phone call.

659
00:40:35,325 --> 00:40:37,327
There was a lot going on.

660
00:40:40,263 --> 00:40:41,598
Okay, well,

661
00:40:42,365 --> 00:40:45,035
please let us know
if you remember anything, or...

662
00:40:45,669 --> 00:40:47,771
if any further information
comes to light.

663
00:40:48,672 --> 00:40:50,073
As you can imagine,

664
00:40:50,874 --> 00:40:54,077
your father's murder
is our highest priority.

665
00:40:55,679 --> 00:40:57,047
Of course.

666
00:40:58,749 --> 00:41:01,017
(tense music)

667
00:41:15,732 --> 00:41:17,634
(indistinct murmuring)

668
00:41:17,734 --> 00:41:20,203
(running footsteps)

669
00:41:25,241 --> 00:41:26,810
(Angie grunts)

670
00:41:26,910 --> 00:41:28,879
(Cole shushing)

671
00:41:28,979 --> 00:41:30,747
(Cole) You're okay. Trust me.

672
00:41:31,581 --> 00:41:34,818
(Angie gasps, breathing heavily)

673
00:41:35,451 --> 00:41:36,486
(Cole) Open it.

674
00:41:37,087 --> 00:41:38,054
(Angie grunts)

675
00:41:40,323 --> 00:41:42,325
- (door closes)
- (lever handle clunks)

676
00:41:42,425 --> 00:41:43,694
(Angie) Who the fuck are you?

677
00:41:43,794 --> 00:41:45,195
I'm not one of them.

678
00:41:45,295 --> 00:41:46,462
Right now,
that's all that matters.

679
00:41:46,562 --> 00:41:47,630
(panting)

680
00:41:47,731 --> 00:41:49,132
There are people in the hold,

681
00:41:49,232 --> 00:41:50,300
and they're in danger.

682
00:41:50,400 --> 00:41:52,168
They're not gonna kill them,

683
00:41:52,268 --> 00:41:53,636
not when they're making money
off of them.

684
00:41:53,737 --> 00:41:54,738
You don't know
what they're gonna do.

685
00:41:54,838 --> 00:41:56,306
They shot me.

686
00:42:01,912 --> 00:42:02,979
(indistinct radio chatter)

687
00:42:05,682 --> 00:42:09,519
(woman speaks Thai)

688
00:42:09,619 --> 00:42:11,855
(migrants conversing in Thai)

689
00:42:15,692 --> 00:42:16,927
- (gunshot)
- (Dara) Aah!

690
00:42:17,027 --> 00:42:18,328
(migrants screaming)

691
00:42:18,428 --> 00:42:19,662
Check for more.

692
00:42:19,763 --> 00:42:21,531
Everybody, let's go!
Out of the lifeboat!

693
00:42:21,631 --> 00:42:23,399
(screaming continues)

694
00:42:23,967 --> 00:42:25,501
(Angie) We need to help them.

695
00:42:26,469 --> 00:42:27,904
(Cole) We will.

696
00:42:28,004 --> 00:42:30,206
But first, we need to take care
of that wound.

697
00:42:30,306 --> 00:42:32,508
Come. This way.

698
00:42:37,781 --> 00:42:39,315
Down there.

699
00:42:41,384 --> 00:42:44,454
(action music)

700
00:42:54,364 --> 00:42:55,732
(exhales sharply)

701
00:43:00,536 --> 00:43:01,972
(Diego hisses) Shit.

702
00:43:40,844 --> 00:43:43,379
(tense music)

703
00:43:52,522 --> 00:43:54,057
(groans)

704
00:43:56,126 --> 00:43:57,227
Come on.

705
00:44:00,696 --> 00:44:02,565
I found Jonathan's stuff
in a lifeboat.

706
00:44:05,936 --> 00:44:07,603
Josef and Simon are dead.

707
00:44:07,703 --> 00:44:09,372
- What?
- Yeah.

708
00:44:11,808 --> 00:44:13,176
They were serious players,
Captain.

709
00:44:13,276 --> 00:44:15,111
Whoever did this
had to be a professional.

710
00:44:15,211 --> 00:44:17,347
It can't be Ellis.
She's fleet navy.

711
00:44:17,447 --> 00:44:18,982
No combat experience.
And even if she did--

712
00:44:19,082 --> 00:44:21,317
(Marko) Still,
she took you out, right?

713
00:44:23,719 --> 00:44:24,955
Sweep the ship.

714
00:44:25,055 --> 00:44:27,057
Find out who the fuck's came on.

715
00:44:27,157 --> 00:44:28,258
Yes, Captain.

716
00:44:31,895 --> 00:44:33,830
(keypad beeping)

717
00:44:36,833 --> 00:44:38,501
We got a problem on the ship.

718
00:44:39,635 --> 00:44:42,238
(loud whirring)

719
00:44:51,481 --> 00:44:52,615
(grunts)

720
00:44:59,655 --> 00:45:00,790
(Angie) Here.

721
00:45:04,627 --> 00:45:06,596
(headsets beep)

722
00:45:06,696 --> 00:45:10,100
(Angie breathing heavily)

723
00:45:14,337 --> 00:45:16,006
(over headset) I've seen worse.

724
00:45:16,106 --> 00:45:17,707
(Angie) I saw you on the news.

725
00:45:18,674 --> 00:45:20,043
I know you're on the run.

726
00:45:20,476 --> 00:45:22,913
Are you at least gonna tell me
your name?

727
00:45:23,013 --> 00:45:24,347
Cole Reed.

728
00:45:24,447 --> 00:45:26,516
(sighs) Okay, Cole Reed.

729
00:45:26,616 --> 00:45:27,850
I'm Angie Ellis.

730
00:45:29,319 --> 00:45:30,987
Okay, Angie Ellis.

731
00:45:31,787 --> 00:45:33,890
This is gonna hurt.

732
00:45:33,990 --> 00:45:35,458
Maybe you wanna talk,
take your mind off of it.

733
00:45:35,558 --> 00:45:36,692
No. (exhales sharply)

734
00:45:36,792 --> 00:45:37,693
Tell me something
about yourself.

735
00:45:37,793 --> 00:45:39,262
(Angie breathes sharply)

736
00:45:39,362 --> 00:45:41,397
Aah! Fuck me!

737
00:45:41,497 --> 00:45:43,733
- You have a family?
- (breathes sharply)

738
00:45:43,833 --> 00:45:45,601
I have a deadbeat ex,

739
00:45:45,701 --> 00:45:47,637
and the most wonderful
little girl in the world.

740
00:45:49,139 --> 00:45:50,540
What's her name?

741
00:45:50,640 --> 00:45:51,707
(Angie) Violet.

742
00:45:53,076 --> 00:45:54,410
Great name.

743
00:45:54,510 --> 00:45:55,979
How old is she?

744
00:45:56,079 --> 00:45:58,314
(Angie breathes sharply)
She just turned six.

745
00:45:58,414 --> 00:46:00,483
(yells in pain)

746
00:46:00,583 --> 00:46:01,617
- Fuck!
- Try to hold still.

747
00:46:01,717 --> 00:46:03,019
(Angie) Oh!

748
00:46:03,653 --> 00:46:06,489
(Angie grunting)

749
00:46:06,589 --> 00:46:07,991
(relieved exhale)

750
00:46:08,091 --> 00:46:09,359
Fuck, that hurts!

751
00:46:10,260 --> 00:46:11,894
- Oh, fuck.
- (bullet clatters)

752
00:46:11,995 --> 00:46:13,129
(relieved sigh)

753
00:46:13,229 --> 00:46:15,398
Oh, my God. (exhales)

754
00:46:15,498 --> 00:46:17,567
(Cole) Share custody
with Mr. Deadbeat Ex?

755
00:46:19,102 --> 00:46:20,536
(Angie) No.

756
00:46:20,636 --> 00:46:22,005
(inhales sharply)

757
00:46:22,105 --> 00:46:23,339
Oh!

758
00:46:23,439 --> 00:46:25,308
I used to share partial custody,

759
00:46:25,408 --> 00:46:27,610
but then I lost it
when I got fired from the navy.

760
00:46:28,711 --> 00:46:30,780
(breathes deeply)

761
00:46:30,880 --> 00:46:32,815
I promised her I'd be back
more than two days a month,

762
00:46:32,915 --> 00:46:34,985
and I--
I can't even fucking do that.

763
00:46:35,551 --> 00:46:37,553
(sighs) There's still time.

764
00:46:40,390 --> 00:46:42,925
- Okay.
- (grunts)

765
00:46:43,026 --> 00:46:44,527
(breathes deeply)

766
00:46:52,702 --> 00:46:54,304
I need backup
at the engine room.

767
00:46:56,306 --> 00:46:58,374
- Oh. Yeah.
- (Cole) Okay?

768
00:46:58,474 --> 00:46:59,675
- We need to keep moving.
- Okay, I got it.

769
00:46:59,775 --> 00:47:02,678
Yeah. I got it. I'm good.

770
00:47:02,778 --> 00:47:05,448
(loud whirring)

771
00:47:19,062 --> 00:47:20,997
(over headset) She was here.
She couldn't have got far.

772
00:47:21,097 --> 00:47:22,332
Move.

773
00:47:32,908 --> 00:47:34,877
Any fishing boat this far out

774
00:47:34,977 --> 00:47:36,646
would be registered
on AIS, right?

775
00:47:37,180 --> 00:47:38,214
Yes, sir.

776
00:47:38,314 --> 00:47:39,515
Let's check and see what traffic

777
00:47:39,615 --> 00:47:40,983
was near the Artemis's position

778
00:47:41,084 --> 00:47:42,985
- around the time of the call.
- Sir.

779
00:47:43,086 --> 00:47:44,587
And, uh, see
what you can drum up

780
00:47:44,687 --> 00:47:47,457
on this Captain Marko Madsen.

781
00:47:58,134 --> 00:47:59,402
Hey, hey.

782
00:47:59,502 --> 00:48:01,104
What happened in Bangkok?

783
00:48:01,204 --> 00:48:02,772
On the news, they said
you're Campallo's bodyguard.

784
00:48:02,872 --> 00:48:05,408
Did you kill him?
Did you kill those cops?

785
00:48:05,508 --> 00:48:07,043
Why are you on the ship?

786
00:48:07,143 --> 00:48:08,478
That is not what happened.

787
00:48:10,280 --> 00:48:11,614
Right now, all that matters
is we get you

788
00:48:11,714 --> 00:48:13,049
and those people to safety.

789
00:48:14,850 --> 00:48:16,419
I sent out a distress signal.

790
00:48:16,519 --> 00:48:17,720
I don't know if anyone got it.

791
00:48:18,454 --> 00:48:20,290
There's no cell service
on the ship, but I know

792
00:48:20,390 --> 00:48:22,558
that there are sat phones
and radios on the bridge.

793
00:48:22,658 --> 00:48:23,926
Then that's where we need to go.

794
00:48:24,026 --> 00:48:25,095
If we go to the bridge,
every man on the ship

795
00:48:25,195 --> 00:48:26,296
will come running.

796
00:48:26,796 --> 00:48:28,030
(sighs)

797
00:48:28,131 --> 00:48:29,799
We need a diversion.

798
00:48:32,202 --> 00:48:34,070
(tense music)

799
00:48:34,170 --> 00:48:35,505
(Angie) In the last cargo hold.

800
00:48:36,606 --> 00:48:37,673
This way.

801
00:48:42,845 --> 00:48:43,913
It's here.

802
00:48:46,882 --> 00:48:48,951
- (handle clanks, squeaks)
- (Angie grunts)

803
00:48:49,051 --> 00:48:50,420
- (Angie) Ah.
- Here, let me help.

804
00:48:51,087 --> 00:48:53,323
(handle clunks)

805
00:48:54,257 --> 00:48:57,993
(doors squeaking)

806
00:48:59,929 --> 00:49:01,597
(Cole) What about the refugees?

807
00:49:01,697 --> 00:49:03,333
In an emergency,
every section of this boat

808
00:49:03,433 --> 00:49:04,467
can be sealed off.

809
00:49:04,567 --> 00:49:05,735
They'll be safe.

810
00:49:13,609 --> 00:49:15,578
(ripping)

811
00:49:21,684 --> 00:49:23,686
- (lighter closes)
- Let's go.

812
00:49:23,786 --> 00:49:26,356
(tense music)

813
00:49:37,467 --> 00:49:38,901
(indistinct radio chatter)

814
00:49:42,272 --> 00:49:44,807
(fire crackling)

815
00:49:46,409 --> 00:49:51,714
(alarm blaring)

816
00:49:51,814 --> 00:49:53,649
Fire on five. Seal it off.

817
00:49:54,116 --> 00:49:55,885
- Initiate fire protocol.
- (buttons click)

818
00:49:56,786 --> 00:49:57,987
Listen up, everybody.

819
00:49:58,087 --> 00:50:00,290
This is a diversion.

820
00:50:00,390 --> 00:50:01,724
We have a stowaway.

821
00:50:01,824 --> 00:50:04,627
I want two guards
at each tower door.

822
00:50:05,561 --> 00:50:08,898
Diego, I want you to oversee
and patrol the towers.

823
00:50:08,998 --> 00:50:10,900
- Yes, sir.
- (Marko) Mateo,

824
00:50:11,000 --> 00:50:12,302
you go down with the fire team.

825
00:50:12,402 --> 00:50:13,803
I'll surveil the deck.

826
00:50:13,903 --> 00:50:14,970
Yes, sir.

827
00:50:15,070 --> 00:50:17,307
(tense music continues)

828
00:50:19,442 --> 00:50:20,476
(gun cocks)

829
00:50:38,928 --> 00:50:40,095
(crewman)
A fire on the high seas.

830
00:50:40,196 --> 00:50:41,431
That's definitely
the worst thing

831
00:50:41,531 --> 00:50:42,765
you can have out here.

832
00:50:44,967 --> 00:50:46,669
(fire roaring)

833
00:50:46,769 --> 00:50:48,103
Increase pressure!

834
00:50:56,446 --> 00:50:57,713
- (loud clang)
- (exhales)

835
00:50:59,815 --> 00:51:02,017
(fire continues roaring)

836
00:51:02,117 --> 00:51:03,886
- It's the batteries, sir.
- (Marko over radio) Contain it.

837
00:51:03,986 --> 00:51:05,120
I'm going up top.

838
00:51:06,722 --> 00:51:09,525
(tense music continues)

839
00:51:14,297 --> 00:51:16,732
(breathing heavily)

840
00:51:47,397 --> 00:51:48,698
(loud clang)

841
00:52:12,955 --> 00:52:14,490
(crewman 1 gasps, grunts)

842
00:52:14,590 --> 00:52:16,659
(crewman 1) Aah!
(grunts in pain)

843
00:52:16,759 --> 00:52:18,461
- (grunts)
- (bones snap)

844
00:52:18,561 --> 00:52:20,296
- (body thuds)
- (radio static crackles)

845
00:52:23,466 --> 00:52:24,834
(beeping)

846
00:52:24,934 --> 00:52:26,201
Mayday, Mayday, Mayday.

847
00:52:26,302 --> 00:52:28,571
This is the KMG Artemis.
Please respond.

848
00:52:29,805 --> 00:52:31,607
All posts report.

849
00:52:31,707 --> 00:52:33,142
All posts report.

850
00:52:33,609 --> 00:52:35,144
Portside secure, sir.

851
00:52:35,244 --> 00:52:36,546
(crewman 2 over radio) Starboard
entrance is secure, sir.

852
00:52:36,646 --> 00:52:39,114
This is the KMG Artemis.
Please respond.

853
00:52:39,214 --> 00:52:40,383
(Mateo) Fire contained, Captain.

854
00:52:40,483 --> 00:52:42,452
Seal the hold. Return to deck.

855
00:52:45,721 --> 00:52:48,558
(Angie) This is the KMG Artemis
on Channel 9.

856
00:52:48,658 --> 00:52:50,259
Please respond.

857
00:52:53,062 --> 00:52:55,130
This is the KMG Artemis
on Channel 16.

858
00:52:55,230 --> 00:52:56,766
Please respond.

859
00:52:57,299 --> 00:52:59,669
Captain to bridge. Report.

860
00:53:01,837 --> 00:53:03,839
We're about to be short on time.

861
00:53:07,276 --> 00:53:08,544
Captain to bridge.

862
00:53:08,644 --> 00:53:09,712
Report.

863
00:53:09,812 --> 00:53:11,581
- Shit.
- (beeps)

864
00:53:15,117 --> 00:53:17,086
(tense music intensifies)

865
00:53:17,186 --> 00:53:18,421
(exhales sharply)

866
00:53:21,156 --> 00:53:23,426
They're on the bridge.
Diego, get up there.

867
00:53:26,161 --> 00:53:27,463
(footsteps)

868
00:53:29,365 --> 00:53:30,600
(Cole) Keep quiet.

869
00:53:31,934 --> 00:53:35,004
(suspenseful music)

870
00:53:46,215 --> 00:53:49,351
This is Captain Spencer
of the USS Hazard Perry.

871
00:53:49,452 --> 00:53:51,120
(Diego exclaims, yells)

872
00:53:52,855 --> 00:53:55,324
(Diego grunting)

873
00:53:57,192 --> 00:53:59,361
(radio feedback squeals,
static crackles)

874
00:53:59,462 --> 00:54:01,096
(Angie) Commander Spencer,
this is the KMG Artemis.

875
00:54:01,196 --> 00:54:02,732
We need immediate
emergency assistance.

876
00:54:02,832 --> 00:54:03,966
(Marko shouting indistinctly)

877
00:54:04,066 --> 00:54:05,568
Who am I talking to
and who is "we"?

878
00:54:05,668 --> 00:54:07,036
(over radio)
My name is Angie Ellis.

879
00:54:07,136 --> 00:54:08,804
I'm the third mate
on the Artemis.

880
00:54:08,904 --> 00:54:11,306
I'm with a man named Cole Reed.
We need help.

881
00:54:12,241 --> 00:54:14,243
The captain is running
a human trafficking operation.

882
00:54:14,343 --> 00:54:16,979
Our position
is latitude 45 degrees north,

883
00:54:17,079 --> 00:54:18,881
- longitude 155 east.
- We need to move.

884
00:54:18,981 --> 00:54:21,383
- Now.
- Send help! Fast!

885
00:54:25,387 --> 00:54:26,956
(Yates) Was that gunfire, sir?

886
00:54:27,056 --> 00:54:28,591
Get me that dossier. Now.

887
00:54:28,691 --> 00:54:30,626
- Set course for the Artemis.
- Yes, sir.

888
00:54:30,726 --> 00:54:33,429
(tense music)

889
00:54:36,231 --> 00:54:37,900
(Angie) Come on.
We're going to my cabin.

890
00:54:42,104 --> 00:54:43,606
We should be able
to get down from here.

891
00:54:43,706 --> 00:54:45,775
(indistinct radio chatter)

892
00:54:49,211 --> 00:54:50,546
(Cole) They're right outside.

893
00:54:55,050 --> 00:54:58,654
(breathing shakily)

894
00:54:58,754 --> 00:55:00,422
(Angie) If I-- If I don't...

895
00:55:01,190 --> 00:55:02,424
Oh, God.

896
00:55:02,525 --> 00:55:03,726
(Cole) Here, sit.

897
00:55:05,928 --> 00:55:07,763
- Look at me.
- (continues breathing shakily)

898
00:55:07,863 --> 00:55:09,264
I'm gonna get you back to her.

899
00:55:10,265 --> 00:55:11,400
I promise.

900
00:55:12,267 --> 00:55:14,604
Mm. Okay.

901
00:55:14,704 --> 00:55:16,939
(tense music continues)

902
00:55:26,749 --> 00:55:28,117
Bigger cut for each of us.

903
00:55:30,052 --> 00:55:31,721
All right, listen up.

904
00:55:31,821 --> 00:55:33,188
There is no stowaway.

905
00:55:33,288 --> 00:55:34,657
That's Campallo's bodyguard.

906
00:55:35,224 --> 00:55:37,159
(over radio)
So, there's a change of plans.

907
00:55:37,259 --> 00:55:40,195
Going in two hours,
ship to ship.

908
00:55:40,295 --> 00:55:41,864
- What's in two hours?
- I don't know.

909
00:55:41,964 --> 00:55:43,465
- (Marko) Understood?
- (all) Yes, sir.

910
00:55:43,566 --> 00:55:44,500
Move.

911
00:55:55,978 --> 00:55:58,748
(phone buzzing)

912
00:56:01,450 --> 00:56:03,052
Go ahead.

913
00:56:03,152 --> 00:56:04,353
(Marko over phone)
What the fuck is Cole Reed

914
00:56:04,453 --> 00:56:06,421
doing on my ship, huh?

915
00:56:06,522 --> 00:56:08,290
How is he even alive?

916
00:56:09,024 --> 00:56:11,126
I thought we took care of him
when we killed Tibu.

917
00:56:12,094 --> 00:56:13,262
What the fuck's going on?

918
00:56:14,997 --> 00:56:17,332
Look, the kill team fucked up.

919
00:56:18,367 --> 00:56:20,903
Don't let him fuck up
the transaction.

920
00:56:21,003 --> 00:56:23,505
He won't.
We moved up the delivery.

921
00:56:23,606 --> 00:56:25,207
I've contacted Bertus.

922
00:56:25,307 --> 00:56:27,109
He's two hours away.

923
00:56:27,209 --> 00:56:28,177
Fine.

924
00:56:28,711 --> 00:56:30,212
Just make sure that Cole Reed

925
00:56:30,312 --> 00:56:32,081
doesn't get off that ship alive.

926
00:56:32,181 --> 00:56:33,415
I will.

927
00:56:33,515 --> 00:56:34,584
You're gonna owe me extra

928
00:56:34,684 --> 00:56:36,185
for dealing with this thug.

929
00:56:36,285 --> 00:56:38,120
Any updates on Kameron?

930
00:56:38,721 --> 00:56:40,455
Are we still in business?

931
00:56:41,190 --> 00:56:42,491
The sale has been halted.

932
00:56:43,626 --> 00:56:44,860
It's business as usual.

933
00:56:46,629 --> 00:56:47,697
What is it?

934
00:56:47,797 --> 00:56:48,898
Who's Kameron?

935
00:56:50,065 --> 00:56:51,366
Kameron's Tibu's son.

936
00:56:51,466 --> 00:56:52,902
And you think he's involved?

937
00:56:53,002 --> 00:56:54,069
I don't know.

938
00:56:55,004 --> 00:56:56,405
But Marko's involved.

939
00:56:57,206 --> 00:56:58,574
- And he's gonna pay.
- (crewman) Move.

940
00:56:59,742 --> 00:57:01,076
Couldn't have got far.

941
00:57:01,877 --> 00:57:03,312
It's time to go.

942
00:57:08,150 --> 00:57:11,186
(tense music)

943
00:57:12,888 --> 00:57:14,256
(Angie grunts)

944
00:57:14,356 --> 00:57:15,925
(gunshots)

945
00:57:19,161 --> 00:57:21,597
(wind whooshing)

946
00:57:27,169 --> 00:57:29,939
(Cole) Until the navy gets here,
those migrants aren't safe.

947
00:57:30,372 --> 00:57:31,807
We need to get below deck.

948
00:57:31,907 --> 00:57:33,308
There are lots of places
to hide 'em down there,

949
00:57:33,408 --> 00:57:34,509
but you heard him,

950
00:57:34,610 --> 00:57:35,745
they're all being guarded.

951
00:57:36,612 --> 00:57:37,913
There's gotta be another way.

952
00:57:39,348 --> 00:57:41,617
We could try
the ventilation shaft.

953
00:57:42,918 --> 00:57:45,020
Sir, the dossier you requested.

954
00:57:45,621 --> 00:57:48,590
Marko's been with KMG
for 13 years, captain for ten.

955
00:57:49,124 --> 00:57:50,760
Danish national, Jaeger Corps.

956
00:57:50,860 --> 00:57:52,161
Tours in Afghanistan, Iraq.

957
00:57:52,261 --> 00:57:53,629
Investigated twice.

958
00:57:53,729 --> 00:57:55,530
Allegations of looting
and smuggling.

959
00:57:56,098 --> 00:57:58,167
They thought he killed one
of his teammates on a mission,

960
00:57:58,267 --> 00:57:59,635
but the rest of the unit
wasn't talking.

961
00:57:59,735 --> 00:58:01,804
- Nothing stuck.
- And his crew?

962
00:58:01,904 --> 00:58:05,174
Half of them are either
ex-military or ex-mercenary.

963
00:58:05,274 --> 00:58:06,709
Spanish MEO,

964
00:58:06,809 --> 00:58:09,344
Irish AOW, GRU.

965
00:58:09,444 --> 00:58:11,280
What about the man
that Angie said she was with,

966
00:58:11,380 --> 00:58:12,915
uh, Cole Reed?

967
00:58:13,015 --> 00:58:15,050
- Anything on him?
- Not on the company roster.

968
00:58:15,150 --> 00:58:16,952
But wait till you see this.

969
00:58:17,052 --> 00:58:18,520
(reporter on monitor)
The suspect is very dangerous

970
00:58:18,620 --> 00:58:20,222
and still on the loose.

971
00:58:20,322 --> 00:58:22,557
A citywide order to shelter
is in place

972
00:58:22,658 --> 00:58:24,994
until he is apprehended.

973
00:58:25,094 --> 00:58:27,096
A cop-killing fugitive.

974
00:58:27,897 --> 00:58:29,564
You have gotta be kidding me.

975
00:58:30,632 --> 00:58:32,835
Just what this shitshow
was missing.

976
00:58:34,436 --> 00:58:36,238
Get me satellite footage
of that ship.

977
00:58:36,338 --> 00:58:37,572
(Yates) Yes, sir.

978
00:58:38,407 --> 00:58:40,910
(metal creaking)

979
00:58:44,146 --> 00:58:45,347
(Angie grunts, strains)

980
00:58:45,447 --> 00:58:47,649
(wind whooshing)

981
00:58:47,750 --> 00:58:48,784
(Angie grunts)

982
00:58:55,490 --> 00:58:57,960
(action music)

983
00:59:02,464 --> 00:59:03,532
(Cole grunts)

984
00:59:08,003 --> 00:59:09,805
(Spencer) Well, shit.

985
00:59:11,273 --> 00:59:13,042
Tell me that's not an MP5.

986
00:59:14,443 --> 00:59:15,544
Sir.

987
00:59:16,145 --> 00:59:18,147
I hear there's a fugitive
on board.

988
00:59:18,881 --> 00:59:19,982
We know if he's a friendly?

989
00:59:21,183 --> 00:59:22,617
Friendly or not,

990
00:59:22,718 --> 00:59:24,419
make sure your men
are good to go.

991
00:59:24,519 --> 00:59:26,121
We launch
as soon as they're ready.

992
00:59:27,356 --> 00:59:28,323
Sir.

993
00:59:32,694 --> 00:59:34,063
(action music continues)

994
00:59:34,163 --> 00:59:35,130
(strains)

995
00:59:43,072 --> 00:59:45,074
(crewman) I think
I heard something over here.

996
00:59:46,976 --> 00:59:49,578
- Over there!
- Cole, someone's coming.

997
00:59:49,678 --> 00:59:51,881
- (metal creaking)
- (flashlight button clicks)

998
00:59:51,981 --> 00:59:54,216
(tense music)

999
00:59:58,988 --> 01:00:01,824
- (gunshots)
- (bullets ricocheting)

1000
01:00:02,892 --> 01:00:05,360
- (scraping)
- Shit! (grunting)

1001
01:00:10,699 --> 01:00:13,168
(panting)

1002
01:00:16,705 --> 01:00:19,574
(wind whooshing)

1003
01:00:26,015 --> 01:00:28,117
(metal creaking)

1004
01:00:30,019 --> 01:00:31,553
(Cole breathing heavily)

1005
01:00:52,908 --> 01:00:53,909
(metal creaks)

1006
01:00:55,277 --> 01:00:57,546
(breathing heavily)

1007
01:00:57,646 --> 01:00:58,881
(thuds lightly)

1008
01:00:58,981 --> 01:01:00,615
(clanging echoes)

1009
01:01:02,317 --> 01:01:05,787
(gunshots)

1010
01:01:05,888 --> 01:01:08,557
(scraping, creaking)

1011
01:01:08,657 --> 01:01:09,658
(muffled thud)

1012
01:01:11,593 --> 01:01:13,495
(metal groaning)

1013
01:01:13,595 --> 01:01:14,830
(cover clatters)

1014
01:01:28,743 --> 01:01:29,945
(Angie grunts)

1015
01:01:31,613 --> 01:01:32,681
Now, we're even.

1016
01:01:36,785 --> 01:01:38,353
(crewman over radio)
Captain, we shot the stowaway

1017
01:01:38,453 --> 01:01:40,222
through the vent shaft,
heard him drop.

1018
01:01:40,322 --> 01:01:41,523
Don't know if we hit him.

1019
01:01:41,623 --> 01:01:42,657
(Marko) Block the hole.

1020
01:01:42,757 --> 01:01:44,226
Return to deck.

1021
01:01:44,326 --> 01:01:46,561
I'll take care
of this guy myself.

1022
01:01:46,661 --> 01:01:47,629
Copy.

1023
01:01:49,498 --> 01:01:51,533
(Angie exhales sharply) Fuck.

1024
01:01:51,633 --> 01:01:52,868
(glass crunches)

1025
01:01:54,369 --> 01:01:55,470
Oh.

1026
01:01:58,840 --> 01:02:00,509
I'd like to see you twirl now.

1027
01:02:01,343 --> 01:02:02,477
Sit down.

1028
01:02:04,479 --> 01:02:05,948
The four of you, with me.

1029
01:02:06,048 --> 01:02:08,918
- Everybody else, fan out.
- (crunches)

1030
01:02:09,451 --> 01:02:11,086
- You keep an eye on her.
- Yes, sir.

1031
01:02:11,186 --> 01:02:12,854
(Marko) Let's go.

1032
01:02:12,955 --> 01:02:14,223
(Spencer) How far are we?

1033
01:02:14,323 --> 01:02:15,357
(Turner) Forty-two miles, sir.

1034
01:02:15,457 --> 01:02:16,391
Time?

1035
01:02:16,491 --> 01:02:18,060
Seventy-five minutes, sir.

1036
01:02:18,860 --> 01:02:19,962
Launch the VBSS crew.

1037
01:02:20,062 --> 01:02:21,230
Yes, sir.

1038
01:02:21,330 --> 01:02:24,166
(action music)

1039
01:02:27,569 --> 01:02:28,570
(hatch opens)

1040
01:02:29,238 --> 01:02:31,840
(engine revving)

1041
01:02:51,193 --> 01:02:52,727
(action music continues)

1042
01:02:52,827 --> 01:02:55,097
(engine revving)

1043
01:03:17,186 --> 01:03:19,088
(exhales sharply)

1044
01:03:19,854 --> 01:03:22,958
- (gunshot)
- (electricity crackling)

1045
01:03:23,058 --> 01:03:27,529
(alarm blaring)

1046
01:03:29,931 --> 01:03:31,800
(alarm continues blaring)

1047
01:03:31,900 --> 01:03:34,369
(suspenseful music)

1048
01:03:35,070 --> 01:03:36,205
(inhales)

1049
01:03:57,459 --> 01:04:01,997
(alarm blaring faintly)

1050
01:04:02,097 --> 01:04:06,468
(blaring intensifies)

1051
01:04:09,471 --> 01:04:11,340
- (squeaks)
- (lock clicks)

1052
01:04:11,440 --> 01:04:12,641
(exhales loudly)

1053
01:04:12,741 --> 01:04:14,009
He's trapped.

1054
01:04:14,109 --> 01:04:15,410
We'll deal with him later.

1055
01:04:16,145 --> 01:04:17,346
Captain to bridge.

1056
01:04:18,080 --> 01:04:20,415
- Lock off cargo hold three.
- (crewman over radio) Sir.

1057
01:04:26,021 --> 01:04:28,790
- (metal groaning)
- (straining)

1058
01:04:33,295 --> 01:04:35,630
- (groaning continues)
- (straining)

1059
01:04:36,498 --> 01:04:39,868
(groaning continues)

1060
01:04:44,206 --> 01:04:45,374
(thud)

1061
01:04:47,042 --> 01:04:50,712
(clattering)

1062
01:04:52,881 --> 01:04:55,784
(clanging)

1063
01:04:55,884 --> 01:04:57,018
(grunts)

1064
01:04:57,119 --> 01:05:00,722
(thudding, clanging)

1065
01:05:00,822 --> 01:05:02,691
Got the intel package
on Cole Reed.

1066
01:05:02,791 --> 01:05:03,858
That'll be all.

1067
01:05:06,128 --> 01:05:08,563
(Underwood) Cole Reed,
born and raised in London.

1068
01:05:08,663 --> 01:05:10,199
Mom passed when he was seven.

1069
01:05:10,299 --> 01:05:12,367
Father was a cop.
Grandfather was a cop.

1070
01:05:12,467 --> 01:05:14,703
Finishes school,
goes right into the navy.

1071
01:05:14,803 --> 01:05:16,037
Royal Marines Commando.

1072
01:05:16,138 --> 01:05:17,872
Two tours in Afghanistan.

1073
01:05:17,972 --> 01:05:20,442
Comes home,
joins the London police.

1074
01:05:20,542 --> 01:05:23,778
Police Combat Cross for acts
of extraordinary heroism

1075
01:05:23,878 --> 01:05:25,380
while engaged
in personal combat

1076
01:05:25,480 --> 01:05:26,948
with an armed adversary.

1077
01:05:27,048 --> 01:05:28,617
Meritorious Police Duty Award

1078
01:05:28,717 --> 01:05:30,452
for an act
of extraordinary bravery

1079
01:05:30,552 --> 01:05:32,887
intelligently performed
in the line of duty.

1080
01:05:35,490 --> 01:05:37,259
Ends up serving under his dad

1081
01:05:37,359 --> 01:05:40,829
in the high-speed SCO19
Specialist Firearms Command.

1082
01:05:41,396 --> 01:05:43,232
His unit was stalking
a mob operation.

1083
01:05:43,332 --> 01:05:45,500
On the takedown night,
Reed went too far,

1084
01:05:45,600 --> 01:05:48,069
disobeyed orders,
got himself stuck inside.

1085
01:05:48,537 --> 01:05:51,606
His father went in to save him
and was shot and killed.

1086
01:05:52,341 --> 01:05:53,342
Wait a second.

1087
01:05:53,442 --> 01:05:54,576
His father was killed

1088
01:05:54,676 --> 01:05:55,677
saving him?

1089
01:05:55,777 --> 01:05:56,945
(Underwood) Yes, sir.

1090
01:05:57,712 --> 01:05:58,847
(Spencer) Jesus.

1091
01:06:00,715 --> 01:06:02,784
So, why'd he leave the UK?

1092
01:06:02,884 --> 01:06:04,353
(Underwood) File goes cold.

1093
01:06:04,453 --> 01:06:05,954
A lot of people looking
for payback,

1094
01:06:06,054 --> 01:06:08,957
and, well...
he has no family left.

1095
01:06:09,057 --> 01:06:11,360
(Spencer breathes deeply)

1096
01:06:12,527 --> 01:06:16,030
I'll bet my pension
and my '67 Shelby

1097
01:06:16,131 --> 01:06:18,567
that whoever killed Campallo
is on that boat...

1098
01:06:19,901 --> 01:06:22,137
and Cole Reed is there
to square things up.

1099
01:06:22,237 --> 01:06:24,473
(tense music)

1100
01:06:31,045 --> 01:06:35,584
(singing in Thai)

1101
01:06:40,989 --> 01:06:43,525
(breathes heavily)

1102
01:06:43,625 --> 01:06:46,395
(breathes sharply)

1103
01:06:57,406 --> 01:07:01,776
(metal squeaks, creaking)

1104
01:07:02,644 --> 01:07:03,812
(gasps softly)

1105
01:07:06,615 --> 01:07:10,319
(ship horn blaring)

1106
01:07:15,257 --> 01:07:18,627
(ship horn blaring)

1107
01:07:32,874 --> 01:07:35,444
- (thudding)
- (sniffles)

1108
01:07:47,289 --> 01:07:48,623
(Marko) Lower the gangway.

1109
01:07:49,391 --> 01:07:50,692
- Lowering gangway.
- (button clicks)

1110
01:07:51,293 --> 01:07:53,895
(whirring)

1111
01:08:00,669 --> 01:08:02,804
(metal groaning)

1112
01:08:07,709 --> 01:08:09,811
(squeaks)

1113
01:08:13,415 --> 01:08:15,984
(phone ringtone playing)

1114
01:08:19,220 --> 01:08:20,422
Did the funds hit?

1115
01:08:25,827 --> 01:08:27,629
Funds confirmed.

1116
01:08:27,729 --> 01:08:30,064
What about our problem?

1117
01:08:31,900 --> 01:08:33,402
It's been contained.

1118
01:08:39,341 --> 01:08:40,842
Let's go and meet our guests.

1119
01:08:42,844 --> 01:08:45,847
(intriguing music)

1120
01:08:58,527 --> 01:08:59,728
Take them to the cargo.

1121
01:09:02,531 --> 01:09:04,866
- Ah, Cap.
- (Marko) Bertus.

1122
01:09:04,966 --> 01:09:06,368
(Bertus) Let's do it.

1123
01:09:06,935 --> 01:09:09,304
I saw smoke coming
from your ship on the way in.

1124
01:09:10,639 --> 01:09:11,973
Oh, yeah?

1125
01:09:12,073 --> 01:09:13,041
Well, what happens on my ship

1126
01:09:13,141 --> 01:09:14,175
is none of your business.

1127
01:09:14,275 --> 01:09:15,310
(Bertus chuckles)

1128
01:09:17,979 --> 01:09:20,114
- You wanna do this or what?
- Yeah.

1129
01:09:20,214 --> 01:09:21,583
Let's go inspect the goods.

1130
01:09:23,117 --> 01:09:24,919
I need to find myself
a clean one.

1131
01:09:25,987 --> 01:09:28,056
Best part of this job
is the ride home.

1132
01:09:28,990 --> 01:09:31,326
- Get in.
- (woman yelps)

1133
01:09:31,426 --> 01:09:32,427
Move.

1134
01:09:35,964 --> 01:09:37,098
(crewman) Get in there.

1135
01:09:47,676 --> 01:09:50,579
(thudding, clattering)

1136
01:09:50,679 --> 01:09:51,780
Thank you, Tibu.

1137
01:09:54,416 --> 01:09:57,085
(straining)

1138
01:10:00,321 --> 01:10:01,756
(sighs)

1139
01:10:02,591 --> 01:10:04,526
(metal creaking)

1140
01:10:05,293 --> 01:10:08,463
(action music)

1141
01:10:21,175 --> 01:10:23,478
(engine rumbling)

1142
01:10:25,547 --> 01:10:27,849
(grunting)

1143
01:10:43,698 --> 01:10:46,234
(light bulb buzzing)

1144
01:10:56,811 --> 01:10:59,080
(suspenseful music)

1145
01:11:04,819 --> 01:11:07,255
(ominous music)

1146
01:11:09,390 --> 01:11:12,393
(breathing sharply)

1147
01:11:16,598 --> 01:11:18,800
(grunting)

1148
01:11:18,900 --> 01:11:21,736
- Aah! (grunting)
- (strap creaking)

1149
01:11:21,836 --> 01:11:23,071
- (Cole grunts)
- (body thuds)

1150
01:11:23,171 --> 01:11:26,040
(intense music)

1151
01:11:31,513 --> 01:11:32,447
(Angie grunts)

1152
01:11:37,719 --> 01:11:38,787
(woman whimpering)

1153
01:11:38,887 --> 01:11:39,921
Here they are.

1154
01:11:42,023 --> 01:11:43,625
Now, get 'em off my ship.

1155
01:11:45,627 --> 01:11:46,928
- (crewmen grunt)
- (body thuds)

1156
01:11:47,028 --> 01:11:48,129
(gun cocks)

1157
01:11:48,229 --> 01:11:49,430
(Bertus)
What the fuck is going on?

1158
01:11:49,531 --> 01:11:51,432
(migrants gasp, whimper)

1159
01:11:56,237 --> 01:11:57,572
We have a stowaway.

1160
01:11:58,406 --> 01:11:59,708
A stowaway?

1161
01:11:59,808 --> 01:12:00,809
Yeah.

1162
01:12:01,275 --> 01:12:02,544
Well, what happens on your ship

1163
01:12:02,644 --> 01:12:04,378
is my fucking business now.

1164
01:12:04,479 --> 01:12:05,547
Calm down.

1165
01:12:05,647 --> 01:12:08,382
Everybody, calm down. Okay?

1166
01:12:08,483 --> 01:12:10,451
I will fix it. Calm down.

1167
01:12:12,386 --> 01:12:16,124
Boys, go down
and take care of this guy. Now.

1168
01:12:16,224 --> 01:12:17,726
Go! Go, go, go!

1169
01:12:19,460 --> 01:12:21,162
Mateo, go to the bridge

1170
01:12:21,262 --> 01:12:23,197
and deal with that bitch
once and for all.

1171
01:12:23,297 --> 01:12:24,999
- You understand?
- Yes, sir.

1172
01:12:27,301 --> 01:12:28,670
(clunks)

1173
01:12:28,770 --> 01:12:30,304
(door groaning)

1174
01:12:31,740 --> 01:12:34,075
(breathing sharply)

1175
01:12:35,577 --> 01:12:36,911
(door groans)

1176
01:12:37,011 --> 01:12:37,979
(gasps)

1177
01:12:44,919 --> 01:12:47,088
- (crewman grunting)
- (gunshots)

1178
01:12:47,188 --> 01:12:48,489
- (blood spurts)
- (body thuds)

1179
01:12:49,357 --> 01:12:52,026
(tense music)

1180
01:13:05,039 --> 01:13:06,708
(Angie grunts)

1181
01:13:09,544 --> 01:13:11,045
(indistinct radio chatter)

1182
01:13:12,714 --> 01:13:14,248
(crunches)

1183
01:13:14,348 --> 01:13:17,451
(crewman yelling,
grunts in pain)

1184
01:13:17,552 --> 01:13:20,722
- (crewman groans, grunts)
- (glass crackles)

1185
01:13:23,457 --> 01:13:26,060
(panting)

1186
01:13:27,161 --> 01:13:29,864
(running footsteps)

1187
01:13:30,799 --> 01:13:32,066
- (Mateo) Aah!
- (body thuds)

1188
01:13:32,166 --> 01:13:33,134
Fucker.

1189
01:13:33,568 --> 01:13:35,870
(breathing heavily)

1190
01:13:38,907 --> 01:13:41,242
(tense music continues)

1191
01:13:53,855 --> 01:13:57,759
(grunting)

1192
01:13:57,859 --> 01:13:58,760
Aah!

1193
01:13:58,860 --> 01:14:01,429
(grunting)

1194
01:14:01,529 --> 01:14:04,766
- (Cole grunting)
- (crewman 1 groans)

1195
01:14:06,034 --> 01:14:06,935
(grunts)

1196
01:14:07,035 --> 01:14:08,536
(crewman 2 grunting)

1197
01:14:10,271 --> 01:14:11,339
(grunts)

1198
01:14:12,273 --> 01:14:13,241
(grunts)

1199
01:14:14,442 --> 01:14:15,409
(body thuds)

1200
01:14:17,578 --> 01:14:18,546
(whispering) Shh.

1201
01:14:19,547 --> 01:14:20,649
Go to the stairs.

1202
01:14:20,749 --> 01:14:22,116
I'll go. Yeah?

1203
01:14:36,397 --> 01:14:39,567
(suspenseful music)

1204
01:14:40,368 --> 01:14:42,370
- (exhales sharply)
- (door creaks)

1205
01:14:43,872 --> 01:14:46,140
(grunting)

1206
01:14:47,942 --> 01:14:49,811
(grunting)

1207
01:14:50,411 --> 01:14:51,479
- (bones snap)
- (grunts)

1208
01:14:51,579 --> 01:14:52,747
(grunts)

1209
01:14:55,283 --> 01:14:58,319
(tense music)

1210
01:15:06,627 --> 01:15:08,496
(knife clatters)

1211
01:15:10,832 --> 01:15:13,567
- (gunshots)
- (panting)

1212
01:15:15,970 --> 01:15:17,405
(gun clicks)

1213
01:15:26,915 --> 01:15:28,182
(door groans)

1214
01:15:31,786 --> 01:15:34,188
(tense music intensifies)

1215
01:15:34,989 --> 01:15:35,957
(gunshots)

1216
01:15:42,630 --> 01:15:44,032
(gunshots)

1217
01:15:45,433 --> 01:15:47,101
(gun clicks)

1218
01:15:48,837 --> 01:15:52,741
(both grunting)

1219
01:15:52,841 --> 01:15:54,342
(yells, grunts)

1220
01:15:54,442 --> 01:15:55,844
(Cole exhales sharply)

1221
01:15:55,944 --> 01:15:59,280
(both grunting, straining)

1222
01:15:59,380 --> 01:16:01,682
- (kick lands)
- (grunting)

1223
01:16:01,783 --> 01:16:04,886
- (both grunting)
- (Marko) Ah!

1224
01:16:06,154 --> 01:16:08,957
(Cole yells, grunting in pain)

1225
01:16:09,057 --> 01:16:10,691
- (Marko grunts)
- (Cole yells)

1226
01:16:12,794 --> 01:16:15,229
(Cole straining)

1227
01:16:19,033 --> 01:16:20,401
(grunts)

1228
01:16:20,501 --> 01:16:23,171
(foreboding music)

1229
01:16:33,047 --> 01:16:34,048
(grunts)

1230
01:16:37,585 --> 01:16:39,988
(Marko) Ahh! (grunts)

1231
01:16:40,588 --> 01:16:43,591
(metal groaning)

1232
01:16:47,428 --> 01:16:48,396
(grunts)

1233
01:16:49,663 --> 01:16:52,300
(grunting)

1234
01:16:52,400 --> 01:16:56,137
(grunting continues)

1235
01:16:56,237 --> 01:16:59,007
(yelling, grunting)

1236
01:16:59,107 --> 01:17:00,441
(Marko) Ahh!

1237
01:17:00,541 --> 01:17:03,411
(loud clanging)

1238
01:17:06,747 --> 01:17:08,116
(Marko grunts)

1239
01:17:14,188 --> 01:17:16,858
(straining)

1240
01:17:20,394 --> 01:17:23,431
- (grunts)
- (Marko yelling in pain)

1241
01:17:25,299 --> 01:17:28,302
- (Cole yells)
- (Marko grunts, groans)

1242
01:17:28,402 --> 01:17:31,672
(Cole grunts, coughs)

1243
01:17:31,772 --> 01:17:36,144
(breathing heavily, grunts)

1244
01:17:36,244 --> 01:17:37,946
(Marko grunts)

1245
01:17:42,917 --> 01:17:44,085
(growls)

1246
01:17:48,990 --> 01:17:50,892
You should have died in Bangkok.

1247
01:17:51,625 --> 01:17:53,194
- (hook pierces flesh)
- (Marko yells in pain)

1248
01:17:53,294 --> 01:17:55,496
(both grunting)

1249
01:17:55,596 --> 01:17:57,665
(Marko yells, grunts in pain)

1250
01:17:57,765 --> 01:18:00,468
- (Cole grunting)
- (Marko grunts, yells in pain)

1251
01:18:00,568 --> 01:18:05,639
Aah! (panting, grunting)

1252
01:18:07,275 --> 01:18:09,777
- (Marko growls) Aah!
- (grunts)

1253
01:18:09,878 --> 01:18:12,213
- (grunts)
- (yelling in pain)

1254
01:18:12,313 --> 01:18:14,916
(Marko grunting in pain)

1255
01:18:18,186 --> 01:18:19,153
(grunts in pain)

1256
01:18:20,021 --> 01:18:22,756
(yelling in pain)

1257
01:18:23,591 --> 01:18:24,926
Ah!

1258
01:18:25,026 --> 01:18:26,460
This is for Tibu.

1259
01:18:38,772 --> 01:18:39,840
(spear gun thuds)

1260
01:18:45,947 --> 01:18:46,948
(sighs)

1261
01:18:47,048 --> 01:18:49,517
(dramatic music)

1262
01:18:56,224 --> 01:18:59,193
(bird squawking)

1263
01:19:04,465 --> 01:19:07,368
(bird continues squawking)

1264
01:19:17,411 --> 01:19:20,314
(dramatic music continues)

1265
01:19:29,557 --> 01:19:31,159
(Tully) Stay the fuck down.

1266
01:19:34,662 --> 01:19:36,030
Just stay down.

1267
01:19:37,565 --> 01:19:40,501
Don't you fucking move.

1268
01:19:40,601 --> 01:19:42,436
- Get the cuffs on him.
- (Navy Seal) Yes, sir.

1269
01:19:46,574 --> 01:19:47,741
(Angie) Wait!

1270
01:19:49,710 --> 01:19:50,678
(Navy Seal) Move it.

1271
01:19:50,778 --> 01:19:52,813
(running footsteps)

1272
01:19:52,913 --> 01:19:53,881
(Angie grunts)

1273
01:20:00,188 --> 01:20:01,322
(Angie) I'm not armed.

1274
01:20:02,023 --> 01:20:04,325
- Who are you?
- I'm Angie Ellis. I called you.

1275
01:20:04,425 --> 01:20:05,859
I'm the third mate.

1276
01:20:06,961 --> 01:20:08,296
He has nothing to do with this.

1277
01:20:08,862 --> 01:20:10,264
He saved us.

1278
01:20:10,364 --> 01:20:11,765
(Tully) Where's the rest
of the crew?

1279
01:20:13,134 --> 01:20:14,135
(Angie) They're dead.

1280
01:20:14,235 --> 01:20:16,104
(Tully) How many were there?

1281
01:20:16,204 --> 01:20:19,373
(Angie) About 20.
And the captain.

1282
01:20:21,909 --> 01:20:23,111
Is that Cole Reed?

1283
01:20:23,211 --> 01:20:24,378
No.

1284
01:20:25,246 --> 01:20:26,380
That's my shipmate.

1285
01:20:29,950 --> 01:20:33,454
You're telling us
that that isn't Cole?

1286
01:20:34,388 --> 01:20:36,657
Cole was shot.
He went overboard.

1287
01:20:38,059 --> 01:20:39,093
Ah.

1288
01:20:41,295 --> 01:20:43,664
- So that's how it went down?
- (inhales)

1289
01:20:43,764 --> 01:20:47,301
Yeah, that's how
it went down, sir.

1290
01:20:50,271 --> 01:20:51,772
(Tully) Keep an eye on her.

1291
01:20:53,341 --> 01:20:54,308
(exhales)

1292
01:20:55,776 --> 01:20:56,844
(Tully) Get him up.

1293
01:20:59,513 --> 01:21:01,282
Looks like you had a rough day.

1294
01:21:03,017 --> 01:21:04,252
Let's check you out.

1295
01:21:05,153 --> 01:21:07,821
There are people on that ship
that need medical attention.

1296
01:21:11,859 --> 01:21:13,994
- All right?
- Oh, yeah.

1297
01:21:16,697 --> 01:21:18,299
(Angie) Yes, that's correct.

1298
01:21:19,433 --> 01:21:21,635
I'll be waiting. Thank you.

1299
01:21:25,339 --> 01:21:26,674
They're sending me a crew
to help me

1300
01:21:26,774 --> 01:21:28,176
with the route back to LA.

1301
01:21:29,310 --> 01:21:31,045
(smacks lips)
So it's Captain Ellis now.

1302
01:21:31,145 --> 01:21:32,113
(laughs)

1303
01:21:32,213 --> 01:21:33,581
(Seng speaks Thai)

1304
01:21:33,681 --> 01:21:35,483
(Angie in English)
Yeah, I don't think so.

1305
01:21:36,517 --> 01:21:38,586
Is that Captain Marko's
sat phone?

1306
01:21:38,686 --> 01:21:40,388
It is.

1307
01:21:40,488 --> 01:21:41,922
Does it have a call log on it?

1308
01:21:42,022 --> 01:21:43,124
Of course.

1309
01:21:46,994 --> 01:21:48,729
- (Angie chuckles)
- Thank you.

1310
01:21:52,400 --> 01:21:53,467
Thank you.

1311
01:21:57,471 --> 01:22:00,541
(indistinct chatter)

1312
01:22:02,143 --> 01:22:03,544
(Angie)
So, where will you go now?

1313
01:22:04,378 --> 01:22:06,080
If you go back to Bangkok,

1314
01:22:06,180 --> 01:22:08,048
you know that they're gonna try
and kill you.

1315
01:22:09,750 --> 01:22:11,185
I need to finish this.

1316
01:22:15,823 --> 01:22:17,091
Get home to Violet.

1317
01:22:19,427 --> 01:22:20,994
(chuckles softly) I will.

1318
01:22:24,698 --> 01:22:26,334
(gasps softly) Ah.

1319
01:22:26,434 --> 01:22:29,703
(soft music)

1320
01:22:38,546 --> 01:22:40,148
(Spencer)
Is the Artemis secured?

1321
01:22:40,714 --> 01:22:42,716
(Tully) Yes, sir.
Artemis secure.

1322
01:22:43,284 --> 01:22:45,286
(Spencer) Is Cole Reed secured?

1323
01:22:45,886 --> 01:22:49,089
According to Miss Ellis,
Reed was killed in action, sir.

1324
01:22:49,723 --> 01:22:52,360
Marko and all 20
of his crew killed.

1325
01:22:52,460 --> 01:22:54,094
Twenty killed?

1326
01:22:54,195 --> 01:22:55,363
(Tully over sat phone)
Twenty-one, sir.

1327
01:22:55,463 --> 01:22:56,530
Plus the pirates.

1328
01:22:57,765 --> 01:23:01,034
There was one friendly crewman
we didn't identify

1329
01:23:01,135 --> 01:23:04,872
who appears to be taking off
on the pirate boat, sir.

1330
01:23:06,940 --> 01:23:08,742
(Spencer) Wait a second.
Let me get this straight.

1331
01:23:09,377 --> 01:23:12,313
Cole Reed is KIA,
but you do not have a body,

1332
01:23:12,413 --> 01:23:14,615
and now, there's
this unidentified crewman

1333
01:23:14,715 --> 01:23:17,117
heading off on a pirate ship.

1334
01:23:17,218 --> 01:23:18,719
Do I have that correct?

1335
01:23:19,820 --> 01:23:21,422
(Tully)
Yes, sir, that's correct.

1336
01:23:23,056 --> 01:23:24,658
You want us to intercept?

1337
01:23:26,260 --> 01:23:29,930
Well, since he is not Cole Reed,
he is not our problem.

1338
01:23:31,665 --> 01:23:33,301
I would agree, sir.

1339
01:23:33,401 --> 01:23:36,637
(tense music)

1340
01:23:37,305 --> 01:23:41,575
(cell phone ringing)

1341
01:23:44,144 --> 01:23:45,213
(Cole over phone) It's me.

1342
01:23:45,313 --> 01:23:46,414
Jesus. Where are you?

1343
01:23:46,947 --> 01:23:48,649
I need you to run a number.

1344
01:23:48,749 --> 01:23:49,783
One sec.

1345
01:23:54,422 --> 01:23:55,523
- (keyboard clacks)
- Go on.

1346
01:23:55,623 --> 01:24:00,027
667-213-4777.

1347
01:24:02,263 --> 01:24:03,831
(Taran) Jaran Daniles.

1348
01:24:04,965 --> 01:24:06,033
I'm coming back.

1349
01:24:06,900 --> 01:24:07,968
(sat phone beeps)

1350
01:24:08,702 --> 01:24:11,539
(tense music continues)

1351
01:24:21,114 --> 01:24:22,916
(woman) Such a lovely service.

1352
01:24:23,016 --> 01:24:25,686
I thought everyone did
such a beautiful job.

1353
01:24:25,786 --> 01:24:28,389
(man) The community
will miss him so much.

1354
01:24:30,491 --> 01:24:33,394
(foreboding music)

1355
01:24:36,997 --> 01:24:37,965
Get in.

1356
01:24:41,469 --> 01:24:42,470
(car door closes)

1357
01:24:49,577 --> 01:24:52,313
(Cole breathes deeply)

1358
01:24:55,549 --> 01:24:56,717
You don't understand.

1359
01:24:58,819 --> 01:25:01,088
I just let them use the ships
to transport cargo,

1360
01:25:01,188 --> 01:25:02,390
and they paid me.

1361
01:25:03,257 --> 01:25:04,525
They paid me a lot.

1362
01:25:06,694 --> 01:25:10,331
But I had no idea what they were
really asking me to do.

1363
01:25:10,431 --> 01:25:11,899
You have to believe me.

1364
01:25:14,001 --> 01:25:16,770
And then they stopped asking
and they started threatening.

1365
01:25:17,905 --> 01:25:19,607
And that's when things
got out of hand.

1366
01:25:21,375 --> 01:25:23,844
Multiple shipments every week.

1367
01:25:26,347 --> 01:25:28,081
Why didn't you come to me?

1368
01:25:28,181 --> 01:25:30,451
Because I thought
I had it handled.

1369
01:25:33,454 --> 01:25:35,723
I thought selling the company
would get me out.

1370
01:25:38,225 --> 01:25:40,328
But I never knew that they...

1371
01:25:40,894 --> 01:25:42,563
I didn't think
they'd go this far.

1372
01:25:45,265 --> 01:25:46,867
You got your father killed.

1373
01:25:46,967 --> 01:25:49,236
(sighs, inhales sharply)

1374
01:25:51,639 --> 01:25:53,240
And you're gonna have to live
with that.

1375
01:25:54,542 --> 01:25:55,943
For the rest of your life.

1376
01:25:58,111 --> 01:25:59,613
(inhales shakily)

1377
01:26:04,718 --> 01:26:06,887
(sighs) Take him home.

1378
01:26:06,987 --> 01:26:08,456
(car door opens)

1379
01:26:10,324 --> 01:26:11,291
(car door closes)

1380
01:26:12,292 --> 01:26:15,329
(intense music)

1381
01:26:39,987 --> 01:26:41,622
(loud crash)

1382
01:26:46,360 --> 01:26:48,662
(metal squeaking)

1383
01:26:51,765 --> 01:26:53,767
(engine hisses)

1384
01:26:56,804 --> 01:26:57,971
(car door closes)

1385
01:26:59,807 --> 01:27:01,141
(Daniles groaning)

1386
01:27:06,447 --> 01:27:07,648
(Daniles gasps)

1387
01:27:09,817 --> 01:27:15,288
(grunting, panting)

1388
01:27:16,657 --> 01:27:18,025
Why kill Tibu?

1389
01:27:19,493 --> 01:27:22,262
Tibu dies,
the company goes to Kameron,

1390
01:27:22,362 --> 01:27:25,132
who's compromised,
who we control,

1391
01:27:25,232 --> 01:27:26,900
and our cargo business goes on.

1392
01:27:27,000 --> 01:27:29,236
You mean the human beings
you were trafficking?

1393
01:27:30,370 --> 01:27:33,040
What do you want?
(continues panting)

1394
01:27:33,140 --> 01:27:34,975
Everybody wants something.

1395
01:27:35,075 --> 01:27:37,978
Tell me what you want.
I'll get it for you.

1396
01:27:40,648 --> 01:27:42,315
What the fuck do you want?

1397
01:27:42,983 --> 01:27:44,818
(Daniles grunts)

1398
01:27:52,392 --> 01:27:53,594
Vengeance.

1399
01:27:54,261 --> 01:27:57,330
(intense music)

1400
01:29:34,327 --> 01:29:35,596
(music fades out)

1401
01:29:35,696 --> 01:29:38,365
(tense music)

1402
01:30:47,601 --> 01:30:49,069
(music fades out)

1403
01:30:49,169 --> 01:30:52,205
(unsettling music)

1404
01:31:50,798 --> 01:31:51,832
(music fades out)

1405
01:31:51,932 --> 01:31:54,968
(intriguing music)

1406
01:32:55,328 --> 01:32:57,164
(music fades out)

1407
01:32:59,232 --> 01:33:02,302
(soft music)

1408
01:33:59,126 --> 01:34:00,160
(music fades out)

1409
01:34:00,260 --> 01:34:03,296
(dramatic music)

1410
01:34:54,948 --> 01:34:56,850
(music fades out)